1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Johann Aegidius Bach (9 February 1645 – November 1716) was organist, violist, and municipal orchestra director of Erfurt, Germany. He was Johann Sebastian Bach's uncle, Johannes Bach's son, and the father of compos
2 CONC er Johann Bernhard Bach. He was a viola player and performer in the Stadtmusikanten Kompagnie (municipal musicians band) in Erfurt. He was organist at the Kaufmannskirche and the Michaeliskirche; on 30 June 1682 he was named the d
2 CONC irector of the Ratsmusik (city council music).
2 CONT
2 CONT https://wikivividly.com/wiki/Johann_Aegidius_Bach
