1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Johann Christoph Bach Jr. BIRTH	29 Aug 1676 Eisenach, Stadtkreis Eisenach, Thüringen, Germany DEATH	1738 (aged 61–62) Thüringen, Germany BURIAL	Non-Cemetery Burial, Specifically: Buried somewhere in Thuringia, Germ
2 CONC any  MEMORIAL ID	132887209 · View Source
2 CONT
2 CONT MEMORIAL PHOTOS 0 FLOWERS 8 He married Anna Hoffman, in 1707 or 1708.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was a second cousin to the famous musician and composer, Johann Sebastian Bach. (They shared great grandfathers.)
2 CONT
2 CONT Johann Christoph could play music, but he was not really interested in it, and he did not want to play for people, like most of his ancestors did. Instead, he taught music, but only when he needed some money.
2 CONT
2 CONT Johann Christoph was a vagabond. He traveled around, all of his life, never really settling anywhere, and never really making a home for his family. He lived in various places, in Germany, Holland, and England.
2 CONT
2 CONT He desperately wanted to go to America, and so he and his family lived in a camp near London for many years, trying to secure passage on a ship. But he was never able to do so. They later returned to Thuringia.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was a second cousin to Johann Sebastian Bach, because they shared the same great grandparents (Johann Hans Bach and Ann Schmied). Also, his first cousin was Maria Barbara Bach, who married Johann Sebastian Bach. (Maria's father
2 CONC  was a brother to Johann Christoph's father.)
2 CONT
