1 NOTE {geni:about_me} * Bartholomaeus Bach left Germany with his wife and two children aboard the ship Friendship. The Friendship departed on February 1, 1738, and arrived on September 20, 1738, in Pennsylvania.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT * [http://arslanmb.org/yDNA/Baugh-DNA-Patriarchs.htm Baugh DNA Project]
2 CONT * Bartholomeus "Bartle" Bach (b. ca. 1684, Germany; d. 1738; m. Margretha Albert) 								
2 CONT * Hans Adam Bach|Baugh (b. 1719, Eggenstein, Baden, Germany; d. 1792-1804, (Wythe Co., VA)?; m. Barbara Flohr) 					
2 CONT * Jacob Baugh (b. 1756, (Lancaster Co., PA)?; m. Barbara) 										
2 CONT * Jacob Baugh (b. 1779-1780, VA; d. after 1850, (Lincoln Co., KY)?; m. Ellenda|Eleanor Ware) 							
2 CONT *Godfrey Baugh (b. 1812, KY; d. 1883, KY; m. Susannah Lay) 									
2 CONT * Ansel Baugh (b. 1834, Lincoln Co., KY; d. 1916, Lincoln Co., KY; m. Mary Ann Wall) 							
2 CONT * William Craig Baugh (b. 1854, Pulaski Co., KY; d. 1926, Lincoln Co., KY; m. Mary J. Atherton) 						
2 CONT *William A. Baugh (b. 1886, KY; d. 1965; m. Anna Irene Butt) (FTDNA 304249) 	
