1 NOTE  The BAUGH family information is provided by Frank Deis, a BAUGH family
2 CONT researcher for many years.  He has a Baugh Family website to share his
2 CONT research with other family on the same genealogy quest.  I found Frank in
2 CONT October of 2003 after returning from a trip to the Family History Center in
2 CONT Salt Lake City that followed my annual ASTRO/SROA Meeting that year.
2 CONT  During that trip I located Martin Luther MILLER, Sr's will from Wythe
2 CONT  County and another MILLER cousin Janie DILLION who transcribed the will
2 CONT and posted it to the Wythe County Gen Web page.
2 CONT  BAUGH in Pulaski Co. KY
2 CONT  by Frank Deis
2 CONT  http://www.rci.rutgers.edu/~deis/bau4.html
2 CONT
2 CONT  It is the thesis of this paper that all of the Baughs in Pulaski County,
2 CONT  KY are members of a single family, and are descended from Bartholomaeus
2 CONT "Bartle" BACH who was born around 1684 and lived in Eggenstein, Germany
2 CONT before coming to Philadelphia aboard the Friendship in 1738. The first
2 CONT known record of Bartle Bach is his wedding, listed in the Eggenstein
2 CONT  church record book (ECB) in 1711: 28 July, 1711 "Barthel Bach, frankish
2 CONT blacksmith and Margretha, daughter of Michel Ebert, a citizen and
2 CONT shoemaker."
2 CONT  Since it isn't common knowledge what is meant by "frankish" I should
2 CONT address that point briefly. The Franks were an important German tribe.
2 CONT Charlemagne was a Frank, as was the first elected German king, Conrad I.
2 CONT In 1711 Eggenstein, saying someone is "frankish" means that he came
2 CONT either from the region around Nuremberg and Wuerzburg (eastern
2 CONT Franconia) or the much closer region around Mainz (Rhenish Franconia).
2 CONT Since Bartle Bach was evidently from "out of town" (the records don't go
2 CONT back to 1684, so this can't be checked) we have no birth record for him.
2 CONT
2 CONT  In the Eggenstein church book (ECB) , birth records for four children of
2 CONT Bartle Bach appear, and death records for two of them: Johann Georg
2 CONT (1Feb 1712 - 14 Sep 1712), Eva Catharina (17 Jan 1717 - ), Hans Adam (2
2 CONT Dec 1719 - ), and Elisabetha (Dec 1727 - Oct 1732). The next record of
2 CONT Bartle Bach's family is in German documents (HKR) where he is applying to
2 CONT  emigrate to Pennsylvania. He evidently paid a manumission fee and
2 CONT  departed on Feb 1, 1738. Hacker states that he left with "wife and two
2 CONT children." His arrival is documented in Strassburger and Hinke, vol. I,
2 CONT  pages 225, 228, and 230 (PGP). The ship Friendship arrived Sept. 20,
2 CONT 1738, and the male passengers had to sign various lists. Bartle's age was
2 CONT given as 54 and Adam's as 18. The women, Bartle's wife Margretha and
2 CONT  daughter Eva Catharina, did not have to sign.
2 CONT
2 CONT  There are some interesting facets to the passenger list. There were
2 CONT  "Stober" families living in Eggenstein and its vicinity, and one of the
2 CONT  passengers on the Friendship was Philipp Stober "Stover" 31 years old
2 CONT from Schroeck, a nearby town (HKR). This is interesting because it
2 CONT  appears that Johann Caspar Stoever baptized most of the Baugh babies
2 CONT who were born in Pennsylvania. And the fact that Bartle and his son signed
2 CONT these lists, and the signatures were preserved (PGS), provided a critical
2 CONT piece of evidence that these particular Bach immigrants are connected to
2 CONT the Kentucky Baugh family. The signature of Adam Bach at age 18 is a
2 CONT perfect match with the signature on his will, at age 72 in Wythe County,
2 CONT VA. (The will was drawn up on 9 Jun 1792 and probated on 11 Dec 1804. It
2 CONT is filed under "Adam Bough" but is signed in the old German script, "Adam
2 CONT Bach.").
2 CONT  After the immigration, Bartle Bach disappears from the records. Bartle's
2 CONT daughter, Eva Catarina Bach, marries John Wilhelm Ernst (19 Aug 1739). It
2 CONT is worth mentioning that a Johann Wendel Ernst, a "single tailor" from
2 CONT Spoeck (HKR), a town close to Eggenstein, had come over a year before the
2 CONT Bach family (on the ship William, which arrived 31 Oct 1737)(PGP).
1 SOUR
