2 CONT +George BAUGH
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT * Reference: [https://www.myheritage.com/research/record-1-127118151-7-460/hans-adam-bach-in-myheritage-family-trees MyHeritage Family Trees] - [https://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Jan 23 2019, 4:24:10 UTC'
2 CONC '
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT The fact that Bartle and his son signed the passanger  lists on the Friendship, and the signatures were preserved, provide a critical piece of evidence that these particular Bach immigrants were connected to the Kentucky Baugh fam
2 CONC ily.  The signature of Adam Bach at age 18 is a perfect match with the signature on his will, at age 72 in Wythe County, Virginia
2 CONT (The will was drawn up on June 9, 1792 and probated December 11, 1894.  It is filed under "Adam Bough" but is signed in the old German Script,  "Adam Bach".
2 CONT
2 CONT Adam Bach shows upspelled "Bach", "Boch", ". Bough", etc.
2 CONT
2 CONT Records for Adam show him in Pennsylvania from 1744 to 1772.  The family moved to Wythe County, Virginia shortly before the start of the Revolutionary War.
2 CONT
2 CONT The heirs of Adam Baugh are listed in his will as follows:
2 CONT George and Henry (listed together)
2 CONT George the oldest son of Adam Bough deceased
2 CONT Katharine Stiffy
2 CONT Barbara Hoover
2 CONT Leonard, Michael, &amp; Jacob (listed together)
2 CONT Elizabeth &amp; Mary
