1 NOTE {geni:about_me} A Patriot of the American Revolution for Virginia.  [https://services.dar.org/Public/DAR_Research/search_adb/?action=full&p_id=A131565  DAR Ancestor # A131565]
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Biography==
2 CONT '''Henry S. Back, Sr.''' was born about 1743 in Orange (Culpepper), Virginia, United States.
2 CONT
2 CONT Henry married [https://www.geni.com/profile-34776631975 Elizabeth Back (Hoffman)]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT They had 6 children together:
2 CONT
2 CONT # https://www.geni.com/people/Mary-Back/6000000008648269555?through=6000000008648191362
2 CONT # https://www.geni.com/people/Joseph-Back/6000000103443628134?through=6000000008648191362
2 CONT # https://www.geni.com/people/Benjamin-Back/6000000103443628128?through=6000000008648191362
2 CONT # https://www.geni.com/people/Pvt-Henry-Back-Jr/6000000008647963939?through=6000000008648191362
2 CONT # https://www.geni.com/people/Aaron-Back/6000000002045244193?through=6000000008648191362
2 CONT # https://www.geni.com/people/Lewis-Back/6000000094524129843?through=6000000008648191362
2 CONT
2 CONT He died between 1807 and 1809 in Madison County, Virginia, United States. 
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.geni.com/discussions/233007?msg=1579043
2 CONT
2 CONT There really was a man named Henry Back, who had a brother named John Back, and they really did marry two sisters named Elizabeth and Margaret Hoffman. They were the daughters of John Hoffman and Maria Sabina Folg.
2 CONT
2 CONT But Henry and John's father was John Henry Back (Johann Heinrich Bach). That Back (Bach) family lived about 11 miles southwest of Culpeper, and practically next door to the Hoffman family. The two Back brothers married the two Hof
2 CONC fman sisters, around 1775, probably in a double ceremony. John Back died in 1794, and his widow Margaret moved to Rockingham County, Virginia. Henry Back died in 1809, and his widow Elizabeth moved to Rockingham County to live nex
2 CONC t to her sister. Elizabeth was seen living there, in the 1810 Census Report (with her son Aaron); she was also listed in the 1810 Tax Lists (as "Aaron Back & mother"); and she was listed in the 1815 Tax List as well. Elizabeth Hof
2 CONC fman Back died in Rockingham County, around 1815; her sister Margaret died there, around 1831. Elizabeth Hoffman Back never went to Kentucky, and so she never established the Back (Bach) family there.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
