1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ==Biography==
2 CONT '''John Back (Bach), Sr.''' was born circa 1738 in Culpeper, VA, United States, or more likely, Thüringen, Germany. His parents were [https://www.geni.com/profile-34765518392 John Henry Bach] and [https://www.geni.com/profile-3476
2 CONC 5519616 Anna Maria Back (Hoffman)]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT John married [https://www.geni.com/profile-67312949 Margaret Hoffman] before July 19, 1779 in Culpeper County, Virginia, United States. Together they had the following 5 known children:
2 CONT # [https://www.geni.com/profile-34743091987 Susannah Floyd (Back)]; 
2 CONT # [https://www.geni.com/profile-127904674 Anna Bach]; 
2 CONT # [https://www.geni.com/profile-34798567995 Sarah Back]; 
2 CONT # [https://www.geni.com/profile-34642932102 Frances Floyd (Back)]; 
2 CONT # [https://www.geni.com/profile-34743091980 Elizabeth Embrey (Bach)]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT He died circa 1793 in Madison County, VA, United States. 
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT "Bache" became "Back" at some point
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT *Predicted Y: https://www.familytreedna.com/public/Bach_to_Back?iframe=yresults J-Culpeper Co VA to Wayne Co KY John Back b. 1760 Culpeper VA d. 1845 Monroe Co IN R-M269
2 CONT
2 CONT * https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/167918055/john-back shows his parents as Anna Maria Hoffman  & Johann Heinrich Bach (https://www.geni.com/people/John-Henry-Back/6000000158571535830?through=6000000103443627974 & https://www.g
2 CONC eni.com/people/Anna-Back/6000000158576504824?through=6000000158571535830 and the entity maintaining the memorial has added and maintains ONLY this memorial and posits that this is a Johan Sebastian Bach https://www.geni.com/people
2 CONC /Johann-Bach/6000000008174402366 cousin and they are from Thuringia, not Freudenberg. 
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT Notes 
2 CONT
2 CONT 20 November 1766 John Back purchased one acre from John Bunger "surveyed for John Back adjoining his mill site whereupon his mill house stands" (Culpeper County, Virginia Deed Book E, 204)
2 CONT
2 CONT 16 February 1767 John Back, millwright of Culpeper, mortgaged his mill and other property to William Allason of King George County (Culpeper County, Virginia Deed Book E, 422)
2 CONT
2 CONT 15 February 1768 John Back sol to William Allason land on the Rappahannock River on lease from Robert Beverly, part of a tract called Elkwood, along with the grist mill built by John Back (Culpeper County, Virginia Deed Book E, 52
2 CONC 9)
2 CONT
2 CONT 19 July 1769 John Back of Culpeper County sold a horse and "bote at my mill on the Rapphannock River" to Joseph Blackwell (Fauquier County, Virginia Deed Book)
2 CONT
2 CONT 1779 John Back owned 150 acres in Culpeper County, Virginia ("The Little Fork Colony From Siegen: Culpeper County, Virginia," The Story of Germanna Descendants in Reunion, (1960).).
2 CONT
2 CONT 12 May 1779 John Back signed petition requesting Culpeper County be divided into three separate counties ("Inhabitants: Petition," Culpeper County, 12 May 1779, Legislative Petitions Digital Collection, Library of Virginia, Richmo
2 CONC nd, VA. Legislative Petitions of the General Assembly, 1776-1865, Accession Number 36121, Box 317, Folder 5. Library of Virginia, (https://www.lva.virginia.gov/: accessed 9 April 2019), Virginia Memory > Digital Collections > Coll
2 CONC ections A to Z > Legislative Petitions Digital Collection.).
2 CONT
2 CONT 19 July 1779 John Back and wife Margaret sold 20 acres to Peter Clore for £20. (Culpeper County, Virginia Deed Book I, p 382-384)
2 CONT
2 CONT 14 January 1783 John Back and wife Margaret and Peter Clore and wife Mary sold to John Wayland Jr. 20 acres for £10. (Culpeper County Virginia Deed Book L, p 240-243)
2 CONT
2 CONT 18 March 1803 Margaret Back, John Embry and wife Elizabeth, Anna, Sarah, Frances and Susannah Back sold land that had belonged to John Huffman (Margaret's father) to Lewis Crigler (Madison County, Virginia Deed Book 3, 395)
2 CONT
2 CONT Sources 	
2 CONT "The Little Fork Colony From Siegen: Culpeper County, Virginia," The Story of Germanna Descendants in Reunion, (1960), possible son.
2 CONT
2 CONT [S0040278] Germanna Record No. 5: Ancestry and Descendants of the Nassau-Siegen Immigrants to Virginia 1714-1750, B. C. Holtzclaw, (Memorial Foundation of the Germanna Colonies in Virginia, 1964, Sixth Printing 2002), 38.
2 CONT
2 CONT [S0040277] Germanna Record #3: John Hoffman, 1714 Germanna Colonist and His Descendants, B.C. Holtzclaw, (Culpeper, VA: Memorial Foundation of the Germanna Colonies in Virginia, April 1963, reprinted July 1989), 69.
2 CONT date of administrator's bond, cites WB 1: 27, 44
2 CONT
2 CONT [S0040278] Germanna Record No. 5: Ancestry and Descendants of the Nassau-Siegen Immigrants to Virginia 1714-1750, B. C. Holtzclaw, (Memorial Foundation of the Germanna Colonies in Virginia, 1964, Sixth Printing 2002), 39.
2 CONT date of administrator's bond, cites Madison County, Virginia WillBook 1, 27, 44
2 CONT
2 CONT [S0040277] Germanna Record #3: John Hoffman, 1714 Germanna Colonist and His Descendants, B.C. Holtzclaw, (Culpeper, VA: Memorial Foundation of the Germanna Colonies in Virginia, April 1963, reprinted July 1989), 69.
2 CONT date they sold land together, cites Culpeper County, Virginia DeedBook I: 382
2 CONT
