1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Cousin to https://www.geni.com/people/Pvt-Henry-Back-Jr/6000000008647963939
2 CONT ----
2 CONT Predicted Y: https://www.familytreedna.com/public/Bach_to_Back?iframe=yresults J-Culpeper Co VA to Wayne Co KY John Back b. 1760 CulpeperVA d. 1845 Monroe Co IN R-M269
2 CONT NOT a brother of https://www.geni.com/people/Henry-Back-Sr/6000000008648191362?through=6000000175543259842
2 CONT ----
2 CONT He was born in Culpepper County, VA. and died in Wayne County, KY.
2 CONT
2 CONT "In 1791, Jacob, his wife Sarah, and their first 3 children (Charles, Mary, and Charlotta) left Russell County,
2 CONT VA and migrated to Kentucky with Jacob's cousin Joseph Back (1745-1819) https://www.geni.com/people/Joseph-Back/6000000103443627974 , his wife Elizabeth Hoffman-Maggard, and their children, who came from Culpeper County, Virginia.
2 CONC
2 CONT As both families crossed over the Pine Mountain, through the gap at the Russell Fork of the Big Sandy River,
2 CONT somehow, the two families got separated. 
2 CONT Jacob and his family decided to head south, and they later settled in what became Wayne County, KY. 
2 CONT Joseph and his family headed north, and settled in what became Breathitt County, KY. 
2 CONT Neither family ever saw each other again. 
2 CONT Dr. Wilgus Bach discussed this, in his 1930 book, "Manuscript of Families of the Breathitt County Area.""
2 CONT per Findagrave Contributor: My Genealogy (47515902)
2 CONT
2 CONT Jacob Back 
2 CONT BIRTH	9 Mar 1764 Culpeper County, Virginia, USA 
2 CONT DEATH	Dec 1839 (aged 75) Wayne County, Kentucky, USA 
2 CONT BURIAL	 Pine Grove Cemetery Clinton County, Kentucky, USA  
2 CONT MEMORIAL ID	21664216 
