1 NOTE {geni:about_me} === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT 1774 Was in the Virginian Militia  Virginia Pension  1774 - 1812 Was in Wythe County, Virginia  1812 moved to Pulaski County, Kentucky     FROM "ABSTRACT OF REVOLUTIONARY WAR PENSION FILES" BY VIRGIL D. WHITE.   R627 , Virginia li
2 CONC ne, also served in 1774, applied 16 September 1833 in Pulaski Co., Ky., age 81, born on 19 October (year not stated) in Lancaster Co., Pa.: enlisted in Wythe Co., Va.    Believed to be the Jacob Baugh who witnessed the Revolutiona
2 CONC ry War Pension of Michael Young.  Pension from Virginia for 1774 application # R627       They lived in the area of Wythe County, Virginia from 1774 to 1812, and then moved to Pulaski County, Kentucky following his brother Henry. 
2 CONC  Some of his family mived to Lincoln County, Kentucky and some to Indiana.
