1 NOTE by Frank Deis
2 CONT  http://www.rci.rutgers.edu/~deis/bau4.html
2 CONT  Jacob, wife Barbara, and his family tended to live at a slight remove
2 CONT from the rest of the Baughs. He was in the area which is now Wythe Co. VA
2 CONT from 1774 to 1812, and then he moved to Pulaski County KY following his
2 CONT  younger brother Henry. Some of his family moved to Lincoln County, KY,
2 CONT  just north of Pulaski, others stayed in Pulaski, and some moved up
2 CONT to Indiana. Jacob's family appears rather rarely in conventional records
2 CONT  such as church books or wills, and thus his children have been assigned
2 CONT  on the basis of educated guesswork. Esther Baugh who married Henry
2 CONT Vaught Sr. in Wythe Co. VA in 1795 may be Jacob's daughter. Adam Baugh
2 CONT who married Magdalena and was the father of Jacob b. 1798 and Abraham
2 CONT b. 1801 (KCH) appears to be a son. Other presumed sons include Jacob Jr.
2 CONT (b. 1780?) who married Eleanor Ware, Gasper/Casper (b. 1793?) who
2 CONT married Dorcas Nicholson and then Barbara Reed, Henry (b. 1793?) who
2 CONT married Susannah Derham and/or Delilah Eade, and John (b. 1802?) who
2 CONT married Sarah "Sally" Williams. The sons lived in Pulaski Co., KY, except
2 CONT John who moved to Lincoln Co. KY.
2 CONT  "Abstracts of Revolutionary War Pension Files" by Virgil D. White:
2 CONT  BAUGH, Jacob or Jacob BOUGH, R627, Virginia Line, also served in 1774,
2 CONT applied 16 Sep 1833 in Pulaski Co., KY, age 81, born on 19 Oct (year not
2 CONT  stated) in Lancaster Co., PA; enlisted in Wythe Co., VA.
