2 CONT George and Katharine moved to Russel County, Kentucky.  In the area was another Baugh family Darius and Marcellius Baugh. These men were evidently the sons of an English Baugh, Abraham Baugh Jr. (1773-1833) and his wife Martha Joh
2 CONC nson.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was named in the Will of his Grandfather Adam Baugh Sr.
2 CONT
2 CONT George stayed on the family farm in Wythe County, Virginia when Henry moved to Kentucky.  In his will (1827) he names his wife Elizabeth and his children: George Jr. b. 1870, Henry b. 1781 who married Elizabeth Miller,  Elizabeth 
2 CONC Wiseman b. 1788, Peter b. 1792, Margaret Etter b. 1793, Mary Blackard b. 1796, Davis b. 1800 who married Catherine  and Jacob b. 1803 who married Barbara.  All decided to move to Lawrence County and Monroe County Indiana.
2 CONT
2 CONT 1810 Census he is listed in Beckley County, Virginia [ now West Virginia ] with 5 Boys and 6 Girls.
