1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ----
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Joseph Back, Jr.''' was murdered by members of the Ford family, according to Dr. Wilgus Bach, probably in southwestern Virginia, in 1802. Dr. Wilgus said that "members of the Ford family killed Joseph Back Jr. because he resent
2 CONC ed the name Back as late as 1802. " However, nobody is really sure what that meant. This Ford family was probably related to the William Ford that married Sally Shackleford, as shown in the attached marriage permission letter. The
2 CONC re was a William Ford who became the sheriff of Fayette County, but it has not been confirmed that this was the same man.
2 CONT
2 CONT However, it is known that the William Ford who married Sally Shackleford must have died before January of 1800, because Sally got married to John Killam on 1-26-1800 in Garrard County, KY (her 2nd husband).
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Either he, or his father, witnessed a marriage permission letter, along the Cumberland River, in SE Kentucky on 10-23-1791, between William Ford and Sally Shackelford. Was it William Ford who later murdered Joseph Jr.?
2 CONT
2 CONT {{https://www.geni.com/media/proxy?media_id=6000000186366713821&size=large}}
2 CONT
2 CONT
