1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Lewis Back BIRTH	14 Oct 1787 Culpeper County, Virginia, USA DEATH	unknown McDonald County, Missouri, USA BURIAL	Non-Cemetery Burial, Specifically: Probably buried on his farm in Missouri  MEMORIAL ID	167921099 · Vi
2 CONC ew Source
2 CONT
2 CONT MEMORIAL PHOTOS 0 FLOWERS 1 This Back/Bach family is not related to Harman Back (aka Hermann Bach), from Freudenberg, Germany. A significant amount of documented research proves this.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was the son of Henry Back and Elizabeth Hoffman. After his father died in 1808, his mother, his brother Aaron, and his two sisters moved to Rockingham County, Virginia. But Lewis moved to southwestern Virginia, to Russell Count
2 CONC y, to live with his cousin John Back, his wife Catherine Robertson, and their children. (John was the son of Joseph Back, who was a brother to Lewis' father Henry Back.)
2 CONT
2 CONT Lewis was seen on the 1810 Personal Property Tax List in Russell County, Virginia as owning two horses. He lived with his cousin John and his family, along Copper Creek, near the Clinch River.
2 CONT
2 CONT In the fall of 1810, John Back and his family wanted to migrate to southeastern Kentucky, where John had grown up. So Lewis went with them.
2 CONT
2 CONT They settled along the Poor Fork of the Cumberland River. On June 22, 1812, Lewis married Elizabeth Pennington.
2 CONT
2 CONT Sometime around 1851, Lewis, Elizabeth, and two of their daughters (Rebecca and Katherine) and their husbands (Turner Fields and his brother Stephen Fields) left Kentucky and headed for the Ozark Mountains. By 1860, they were livi
2 CONC ng in McDonald County, Missouri, near Honey Creek.
2 CONT
2 CONT It is believed that they both died sometime between 1860 and 1870. They were probably buried there, on their farm.
2 CONT
