1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Not https://www.geni.com/people/Sarah-Back/6000000147225996858 who married https://www.geni.com/people/John-Back-of-Monroe-County/6000000024322220782?through=6000000147225996858
2 CONT ----
2 CONT Sarah “Sally” Lloyd Back 
2 CONT BIRTH	1763 New Jersey, USA 
2 CONT DEATH	26 Nov 1844 (aged 80–81) Wayne County, Kentucky, USA 
2 CONT BURIAL	Non-Cemetery Burial, Specifically: Probably re-buried in the Pine Grove Cemetery  
2 CONT MEMORIAL ID	167727507 
2 CONT
2 CONT Her father was either John Lloyd or Thomas Lloyd.
2 CONT
2 CONT She married Jacob Back on Dec. 29, 1785 in Abingdon, Virginia. 
2 CONT They migrated to Kentucky with Jacob's cousin, Joseph Back, and his family. 
2 CONT But they somehow got separated from Joseph and his family, as they were crossing over the Pine Mountain.
2 CONT
2 CONT Joseph and his family later settled in what became Breathitt County. Jacob and Sally and their children settled near the Cumberland River, at the forks of Beaver Creek and Otter Creek.
2 CONT
2 CONT Sally and Jacob eventually owned about 1,000 acres of land there.
2 CONT
2 CONT Sally wrote her will on June 29, 1844, a few years after Jacob died. 
2 CONT She died a few months later.
2 CONT
2 CONT It is believed that Sally was buried next to Jacob. However, when the Cumberland Lake was built, the graves that would soon be submerged were moved to the Pine Grove Cemetery. Most of them were marked, including Jacob's grave. But
2 CONC  Sally's grave cannot be found. Either her grave was not moved in time, or else she was re-buried in one of the unmarked graves in the Pine Grove Cemetery.
2 CONT
2 CONT Family Members 
2 CONT Spouse Jacob Back 1764–1839
2 CONT
