2 CONT http://trees.ancestry.com/pt/AMTCitationRedir.aspx?tid=156739478&pid=1465 
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Her father was either John Lloyd or Thomas Lloyd. Some records say her parents were Thomas Loyd (or Lloyd) and Mary Wheelwright. Thomas Loyd was born in 1745 in NJ and fought in the Revolutionary War.
2 CONT
2 CONT She married Jacob Back on Dec. 29, 1785 in Abingdon, Virginia (Washington County). They migrated to Kentucky with Jacob's cousin, Joseph Back, and his family. But they somehow got separated from Joseph and his family, as they were
2 CONC  crossing over the Pine Mountain. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Joseph and his family later settled in what became Breathitt County. Jacob and Sally and their children settled near the Cumberland River, at the forks of Beaver Creek and Otter Creek. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Sally and Jacob eventually owned about 1,000 acres of land there. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Sally wrote her will on June 29, 1844, a few years after Jacob died. She died a few months later.
2 CONT
2 CONT It is believed that Sally was buried next to Jacob. However, when the Cumberland Lake was built, the graves that would soon be submerged were moved to the Pine Grove Cemetery. Most of them were marked, including Jacob's grave. But
2 CONC  Sally's grave cannot be found. Either her grave was not moved in time, or else she was re-buried in one of the unmarked graves in the Pine Grove Cemetery.* Reference: [https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/167727507/sarah_back Find
2 CONC  A Grave Memorial] - [https://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Feb 20 2025, 19:34:51 UTC''
