1 NAME Catherine /Robertson/
2 GIVN Catherine
2 SURN Robertson
2 _MARNM Back
2 NICK Caty
2 NICK Robinson
1 SEX F
1 BIRT
2 DATE 7 APR 1780
2 ADDR
3 STAE Tennessee
3 CTRY United States
1 BURI
2 DATE 1858
2 PLAC Roark Cemetery
2 ADDR
3 CITY Noctor
3 STAE KY
3 CTRY United States
1 DEAT
2 DATE 1 SEP 1858
2 PLAC Quicksand Creek
2 ADDR
3 CITY Noctor
3 STAE Kentucky
3 CTRY United States
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://www.geni.com/people/Catherine-Back/6000000001679959892 is seen as daughter of https://www.geni.com/people/Benjamin-Robertson/6000000009928090192?through=6000000001679959892 & https://www.geni.com/people/Cel
2 CONC ia-Robertson/6000000009927802070?through=6000000001679959892. 
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT She married John Back when she was about 16 years old. They first lived in southwestern Tennessee. Around 1810, they moved to southeastern Kentucky, where John had grown up.
2 CONT
2 CONT There were two excellent books written about this family, and both of them are available from this website: www.BachGenealogy.com
2 CONT
2 CONT She was known as "Caty." 
2 CONT ===Family
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/168583645/john-back
2 CONT
2 CONT While John was in southwestern Virginia, he met and married Catherine Robertson, in 1795. She lived with her family, on the east side of the Clinch River, just south of where John William Back's farm was, in what is now Hawkins Co
2 CONC unty, Tennessee. She had bright red hair. Many of her and John's children also had the same bright red hair.
2 CONT
2 CONT John's best friend Samuel Maggard married Catherine's sister Rebecca, also in 1795. And Catherine and Rebecca's sister Easter married Charles Blair, also in 1795. It was said there was a triple wedding, but that has not been prove
2 CONC n. John's older brother Joseph Jr. also got married in 1795, in Virginia, but the name of his wife is not known.
2 CONT
2 CONT John Back and Catherine Robertson had at least nine children:
2 CONT
2 CONT * 1. Mary Back (born 1797 but died as an infant).
2 CONT * 2. Mary Back (born December 12, 1798) who married John R. Roark.
2 CONT * 3. Catherine Back (born about 1800 but died young).
2 CONT * 4. Joseph Woodford Back (born March 7, 1802) who married Permelia Hogg.
2 CONT * 5. Susannah Back (born September 20, 1804) who married John Henry Holbrook.
2 CONT * 6. Lewis Back (born May 29, 1807) who married Margaret "Peggy" Roberts.
2 CONT * 7. John Back Jr. (born March 27, 1810) who married Elizabeth Cope.
2 CONT * 8. Solomon Back (born July 10, 1812) who married Jincy Fields.
2 CONT * 9. Isaac Back (born May 28, 1817) who married Rachel Combs.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Disputed Origins 
2 CONT
2 CONT According to the Oven Fork Church Minutes, these Robinson Women were all Daughters of Benjamin Robertson and Celia ?.
2 CONT
2 CONT {{https://www.geni.com/media/proxy?media_id=6000000186365012872&size=large}}
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ===References 
2 CONT * https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/21313827/catherine-bach “ Catherine Robinson Back is buried beside her husband, John Back(h). She was described as being red-haired with blue eyes, and of Scotch-Irish descent, however, her pa
2 CONC rents remain unknown. John and Catherine Robinson Back were my G.G.G. Grandparents.”
2 CONT * https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/197586752/catherine-back “Catherine Robertson was the daughter of John Robertson and Margaret King, as shown here, on Find A Grave. Her last name was definitely spelled as "Robertson," and her
2 CONC  lineage within the Robertson family has been well-documented and proven by several professional researchers and genealogists, including Ms. Evelyn Rowland. (You may be able to still find Ms. Rowland's research on the internet.)  
2 CONC It is important to note that, many years ago, in various documents, the last name of "Robertson" was often misspelled as "Robinson," and vice versa. …”
2 CONT * < [https://sites.rootsweb.com/~bachgenealogy/ “Genealogy of the Bach (Back) Family”] >
