1 NOTE {geni:about_me} (Researcher Note by CHCurtis: There are many errors noted in the genealogy of the Back/Bach line in many FAG memorial)
2 CONT
2 CONT He was born in Russell County, Virginia, on a farm that his father and mother had settled on, after they got married in 1795. The farm had belonged to his father's great uncle (Johann Wilhelm Bach, known as John Back), but he had 
2 CONC died in 1794. His parents left Russell County, in 1810 and moved to Kentucky--actually his father was coming home to Kentucky.
2 CONT
2 CONT During the first few years of their marriage, Lewis and Peggy moved back and forth between Harlan County, KY and Russell County, VA.
2 CONT
2 CONT But by 1853, Lewis had bought 1,687 acres in Morgan County, KY--it later became part of Magoffin County. He built a nice home there, which he called "White Pine." He lived there for the rest of his life.
