1 NOTE {geni:about_me} (H/Susan Graves; D/James & Elizabeth Pratt Graves)
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/121234386/mary-back
2 CONT
2 CONT In March of 1806, Mary Back had an affair with John Colyer Jr. (FAG #5172556). He was a stranger to the area, and so she did not know that he was already married. 
2 CONT
2 CONT But John suddenly soon disappeared. Mary was frantic. It was said that Mary thought that he was either "lost in the wilderness" or had been "attacked by wild animals." A few weeks later, she realized that she was pregnant. (She ne
2 CONC ver married John Colyer; he was already married; he had married Susannah Graves around 1803, in Rockcastle County, Kentucky.)
2 CONT
2 CONT Mary's son Alfred Back was born on Dec. 27, 1806. But Mary died, a couple of weeks later, in January of 1807. It was said that she was buried next to her parent's cabin along Collier's Creek, near the Poor Fork of the Cumberland R
2 CONC iver.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT * https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/5172556/john-colyer
