1 NOTE {geni:about_me} WILLIAM ARMSTRONG COOPER, son of Elder Henry Cooper was born in Wayne county, Ky., May 4, 1813. 
2 CONT He was brought up on a farm, and received only such an education as the schools of his neighborhood could afford.But possessing superior natural gifts, he acquired a good stock of knowledge by his own unaided efforts. 
2 CONT At the age of 20 years, he professed hope in Christ, and was baptized into the fellowship of Beaver Creek church, by Matthew Floyd. 
2 CONT A year later, he was married to Sallie Cooper. 
2 CONT He was licensed to exercise his gift, about 1835, and was ordained to the pastoral care of Beaver Creek church, about 1840. 
2 CONT To this congregation he has continued to minister to the present time. 
2 CONT He has also served the churches at Seventy-Six, Clear Fork, Bethel, and 2dNew Hope and Friendship, during longer or shorter periods. 
2 CONT He is regarded a preacher of superior ability, and the esteem in which he is held by his brethren, is evinced in the fact that he has been elected moderator of South Concord Association at least 19 times, has served it as clerk, t
2 CONC wo years, and preached the introductory sermon before it on at least 18 occasions. 
2 CONT During the year 1876, he baptized 450 persons,and he supposes he has baptized, in all, something over 2,000 converts.
2 CONT Cooper Floyd
2 CONT * Reference: [https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/46764184/william_armstrong_cooper Find A Grave Memorial] - [https://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Feb 20 2025, 19:32:57 UTC''
