1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Wayne County Outlook
2 CONT 3 Mar 1910
2 CONT
2 CONT Jacob M. Cooper, aged 85 years,
2 CONT died Feb. 16. He was born and
2 CONT raised on Beaver Creek where
2 CONT he lived until two years ago.
2 CONT
2 CONT He professed faith in Christ early
2 CONT in life and united with the Baptist
2 CONT church to which he was a
2 CONT consistent member until death.
2 CONT
2 CONT He told the writer of his conversion
2 CONT and of his obiding trust in the 
2 CONT goodness of him who cares for us all.
2 CONT
2 CONT During the two last years of
2 CONT his stay on this earth he stayed
2 CONT with his two daughters, Mrs. W.C.
2 CONT Rector and Mrs F. M. Shearer.
2 CONT
2 CONT His last days were spent with Mrs. 
2 CONT W. C. Rector, who did all for him that
2 CONT loving hands could do. But the Lord 
2 CONT saw best to take him from us and we
2 CONT want to be submissive to, the will 
2 CONT of the Lord.
2 CONT
2 CONT Grandpa on his death bed said
2 CONT "Jesus suffered and I must suffer
2 CONT too" and also said "the Lords
2 CONT will be done not mine"
2 CONT
2 CONT His remains were laid beside
2 CONT his wife in the Old Beaver Creek
2 CONT Cemetery.
2 CONT
2 CONT His Granddaughter
2 CONT Florence Rector* Reference: [https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/46766686/jacob_madison_cooper Find A Grave Memorial] - [https://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Feb 20 2025, 19:32:57 UTC''
