1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Hon. A.W. Miller, former county commissioner in Republic County, died at his home near Hollis Thursday night at the age of 65 years.  
2 CONT
2 CONT Mr. Miller served his country during the Civil War as a member of Company G, Fifth Missouri Voluntary Cavalry, being in all the fights and skirmishes in which is company took part. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Mr. Miller was one of the first settlers near the old town of Seapo.  Mr. Miller was active in the work of the county and served as commissioner in Republic County for several years.  Even though most of the land he owned was in R
2 CONC epublic County, he donated the land for the first Hollis school - which later burned.  Mr. Miller was one of the prosperous farmers in this part of Kansas and was a man of fine virtues.  
2 CONT
2 CONT He has spent his winters in California for a number of years and his summers here with his children.  He has three sons and one daughter here, one in Kansas City, one in Washington and one in California.  He is survived by his wif
2 CONC e, Frances, and their children.  One of his daughters is Mrs. John Brightop of Hollis.* Reference: [https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/90294197/anthony-wayne-miller Find A Grave Memorial] - [https://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCop
2 CONC y/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Aug 6 2022, 5:51:22 UTC''
