1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Mary Margaret Myers was born in Wythe Co., VA on May 4, 1802. She married Martin Luther Miller Jr. on July 8,1819 in Wythe Co., VA. She was his second wife.  They had atleast the following children: Rebecca, Isaac 
2 CONC Cass, John Wesley, Amanda, Andrew and Malinda Miller.
2 CONT
2 CONT After the death of Martin Luther Miller Jr. She married James Benjamin Wright b. 1781 in NC and d. 1873 Monroe Co., IN. Mary and James were married on Oct 22, 1835 in Monroe Co., IN. They had the following children: George Johnson
2 CONC  Wright, Susan E Wright, Elizabeth Wright and Lewis Wright. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Mary (age 48) appears on the 1850 Census of Clear Creek, Monroe Co., IN married to James Wright age 69 with one Miller Daughter (Malinda) age 16 and Johnson Wright age 14, Susan age 11, Elizabeth age 8, and Lewis age 6
2 CONT
2 CONT Mary (age 56) appears on the 1860 Census of Clear Creek, Monroe Co., IN with James age 79 Susan age 21, Elizabeth age 18, and Lewis age 10.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mary (age 68) appears on the 1870 Census of Cleark Creek, Monroe Co., IN with James (age 91) daughter Elizabeth Flood, her husband Willis Flood and a Lewis age 10.(not sure if age is enumerated incorrectly or this is an unknown Le
2 CONC wis.
2 CONT
2 CONT After the death of James Benjamin Wright, Mary went to live with her son John Wesley Miller in Nodaway Co., MO. She appears with this son on the 1880 Census age 78 but listed as Mary Wright.
2 CONT
2 CONT On tombstone...It should be noted that Mary is listed as a Miller and not a Wright and married to M.L. Wright. Since she was with her Miller children...they chose to bury her as their mother married to their father. There may have
2 CONC  been hard feelings towards James Benjamin Wright...will never know. But she did have Wright children. Her son  George Johnson Wright named a son Martin Luther Wright. 
2 CONT
