2 CONT
2 CONT === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT Barnabas A. "Barney" Back, born 28 January 1833 in southwest
2 CONT Virginia. He married, first, Minerva Hounshell, 11 December 1853. Shewas born in 1834 in Lee County, Virginia, daughter of Andrew and Vina(Bryan)
2 CONT Hounshell. They lived in the Seitz area of Morgan County, Kentucky,which
2 CONT became part of Magoffin County in February 1860. Barney owned only afew cattle and hogs, and a horse (or mule) or two in 1858/59.
2 CONT Their home was lost in a lawsuit settlement dated 25 April 1869,Daniel Gullet vs. Lewis Back. Barney A. Back promised to pay $650.87,plus six percent interest, to John W. Hazelrigg (Commissioner of theCourt) for land. Isaac Back c
2 CONC o-signed. Apparently Barney did not pay,because Lewis Patrick had him put out by writ of forcible entry,sometime before October 1872. The house that was lost was a one-storylog home with a dug well that was 75 feet deep. A modem h
2 CONC ouse standson the site, where the Paddle and Spruce Pine enter the Right MiddleFork. Minerva died in 1867 and is buried in the Puncheon Cemetery inSeitz; no markerexists.
2 CONT Barney married, second, Susannah Back (75A 6-8), 11 December 1869.Barney was fanning 150 acres on Middle Fork around 1870. Later, he rana grocery store in Jackson with some of his sons. Barney was sick foryears before he died of c
2 CONC ongestive heart failure, 29 October 1903. TheBreathitt News called him a "good citizen." Barney and Susannah areburied in the Lazarus Bach Cemetery, side by side. -- A Back FamilyHistory 2008
