1 TITL Reverend
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Felix Combs' father was Moses Combs. He served in the Civil War as a private in the 13th Kentucky Cavalry, Co. C.
2 CONT
2 CONT He first married Susannah Combs on Nov. 24, 1845. They had at least five children. But she died a few months after giving birth to their son Moses.
2 CONT
2 CONT Seven months later, Felix got remarried to Chloe Bransom. She had been previously married to Ezekiel Hall and Russell Begley. Felix had one child with Chloe.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1894, Felix got married to Sarah (Back) Sumner. She was a widow who had been left with nine little children to raise, after her husband James Sumner Jr. died of typhoid fever in Oct of 1879. She was two months pregnant when he 
2 CONC died. Sarah and Felix lived out the last years of their lives together.
2 CONT
2 CONT It was said that he preached at a local church, near Troublesome Creek. Felix's second wife Chloe is also buried here (Fisty Cemetery, Knott County, Kentucky). It is not known where his third wife Sarah was buried.
2 CONT * Ref: [http://www.findagrave.com/cgi-bin/fg.cgi?page=gr&GRid=61610788 FindAGrave memorial]
