2 FORM jpg
2 _PRIM Y
2 NOTE Broken Laptop was an IBM ThinkPad, the case broke open in a fall (multiple falls and quit working after the last one). My son took the hard drive out to put it in another newer ThinkPad of his to retrieve my files and photos but i
3 CONC t didn't fit and had different connectors. Since then he has moved and now says he did not keep the broken computer but may still have the hard drive... not sure ... will look... hope he finds it. I took photos instead of notes of
3 CONC  what I found because it was so much faster. I do know that Silas Wann (a couple of them ... wife name was only way to tell which Silas) bought real estate ... those records are safe to be seen any time in the current courthouse i
3 CONC n Berryville. But Masonic Lodge Records could be lost forever.
2 NOTE I don't remember anything about confirmations.. mostly rather boring minutes of meetings....anyway a lot of those. Some times names of someone who should or should not be allowed to join and why... those discussions and  decisions
3 CONC  were more interesting and always took a number of meetings to work through their process. I didn't have time to read all the records that I was given access to. I doubt if I or anyone can ever see them again.
2 NOTE tell me about this lap top... how is it broke? does it turn on at all? ok then if he held several offices then he was a freemason most of his life... were there any records of when he became confirmed? Was Silas listed in any of t
3 CONC he records? I need to stop for the night I am sooo consumed with this... i need sleep. its hard to put it down when I start finding great clues. thank you for working with me. have a good morning! T
2 NOTE oh my gosh.... i knew it! ok then was his father and grandfather also Freemasons?  that could be a huge clue at to where they came from...
2 NOTE Yes he was a active leader of the Masons in Carrollton then when the town started to die he joined the Masonic Lodge in Green Forest (the two Lodges then merged). When I was there in 2005 the Leader of the Green Forest Masonic Lod
3 CONC ge let me look through their books from Ike's time there. Ike held about every office position there, I don't remember his titles but I did read a lot of meeting notes that he wrote. The Lodge leader was very sad that the lodge wa
3 CONC s dying for lack of new blood... the younger generation didn't seem to be interested.I took some photos but they are in that broken laptop. Then that mallet in my photo has something to do with the Masons too? Maybe what he (whoev
3 CONC er that is) used to start and end the meeting? I had hoped to find a picture of him, they had no photos... just hand written records.
2 NOTE OK BOBBY I HAVE RESEARCHED THIS ONE FOR WEEK NOW AND I GOT... HE IS A FREEMASON.  MANY WANN MEN ARE MEMBERS OF THE MASONIC LODGE. i AM STILL LOOKING FOR THE LODGE THAT HE BELONGED TO BUT I AM 99% SURE THAT THIS IS THE MEANING. I A
3 CONC M NOT DONE WITH THE SEARCH SO I WILL LET YOU KNOW ABOUT THE OTHER 1% 
2 NOTE I am very curious about the meaning of the banner(?) and the apron he is wearing. Very similar to the other photo. Could the apron be part of his blacksmith uniform and the banner identify his regiment? I am surprised at how young
3 CONC  he looks for 63.
