1 NOTE {geni:about_me} === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT Obituary (Holton Recorder 7-2-1951) - Andrew Harmon Wolfe, son of Silas and Nancy Wolfe, was born September 19, 1877, in Lee County, Virginia. He died at the Holton hospital at the age of 73 years, 9 months, and 9 days.    On July
2 CONC  29, 1889, he was united in marriage to Sarah Elizabeth Edens at Jonesville, Virginia.  To this union were born 12 children; 3 sond and 9 daughters: Calvin of Topeka, James of Netawaka, Harmon of Robinson, Mrs. Lillie McQueen of C
2 CONC ircleville, Mrs. Mae Shupe, Mrs. Bertha Cramer and Mrs. Lennie Coates of Netawaka, Mrs. Belle Hall, Mrs. Hazel Moore, and Mrs. Myrtle Bauer all of Holton, and Mrs. Fanny Ramsey of Topeka and Mrs. Verla Simmons now deceased, also o
2 CONC ne adopted son George Hoenshell of the home.  There are 34 grandchildren and 21 great grandchildren.    He was united with the Christian Church in Lee County, Virginia, at an early age and he has been a member of the Christian chu
2 CONC rch here in Holton since moving to the city ibn 1937.    He was a good and loving husband and parent, so esteemed by his family and others who knew him.    He is buried in the Holton cemetery.
