1 NOTE {geni:about_me} While at work at the National Quarry south of Clear Creek this afternoon, Andrew Zikes, aged 72, of Harrodsburg was almost instantly killed when a stone that was being lifted by a derrick fell.  The accident was du
2 CONC e to the "dogs" slipping.
2 CONT
2 CONT The aged man was struck on the head and had his skull crushed.
2 CONT
2 CONT He is survived by his family.
2 CONT
2 CONT Bloomington Weekly Courier, May 27, 1910, Clipping File, Monroe County History Center, Bloomington, Indiana.
