1 NOTE {geni:about_me} === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT In 1954 she was operated on for cancer of the mouth and a malignant tumor was remover fro the roof of her mouth.  After the surgery she always had difficulty speaking clearly but she could be understood.     The American Cancer So
2 CONC ciety publicised her recovery and for several years she was featured in newspaper articles and at Cancer functions.     At the time of her death she lived with her husband at 202 4th Street,  Piqua, Ohio.  She had 28 grandchildren
2 CONC  and 32 great grandchildren when she died.           Ada Ethel Baugh     Burial Thursday    Mrs Ada Ethel Baugh, 79, of 202 fourth died at 4 am today in Piqual Memorial Hospital.  She was hospitalized for 10 days and in failing he
2 CONC alth one year.    Born July 28, 1887, in Stanfork Kentucky she was the daughter of Mr. and Mrs. Andrew Young.  She has lived in Piqua 38 years since coming here in 1924.  Mrs Baugh was married to Joseph Baugh in Stanford, Ky.  She
2 CONC  was a member of the Christian Church in Stanford.    Surviving in addition to her husband , joseph, are eight daughters, Mrs. Cleda Rittenhouse of Seattle, Wash., Mrs. Paul Williamson , Mrs. James Munk, Mrs. William Supinger, all
2 CONC  of Piqua, Mrs. Ralph McSwain of Palm Springs, Calif., Mrs Robert Alexander of Dayton, Mrs. Paul Ross of Piqua, Mrs Charles Langford of Troy, 28 grandchildren, 32 great-grandchildren; one son Earl Baugh of Piqua; two sisters Erma 
2 CONC Ray, of Lexington Ky., and Ollie Seisler of Stanford Ky.    Funeral services will be at 2 pm Thursday in Madison Home for Funerals.  Rev. Charles Short will officiate.  Burial will be in Forrest Hill Cemetery.    Friends may call 
2 CONC at the funeral home from 2 to 4 and 7 to 9 pm Wednesday.
