2 CONT OBITUARY     Bertha C. Williamson, 78, of 711 Leonard St., Piqua died at 9:30 am Tuesday Oct. 4, 1988, in Piqua Memorial Medical Center.   She was born in Kentucky on April 22, 1910, to the late Joseph and Ada Young Baugh.   She w
2 CONC as married to Paul D. Williamson on July 22, 1960, in Piqua, and he survives her.   Also surviving are one son, Jack Martz of New Symerna Beach Fla; two grandchildren; one brother, Earl Baugh of Piqua; five sisters, Mrs Ollie Supi
2 CONC nger of Piqua, Mrs Charles Langford (Dorothy) of Troy, Mrs. Robert Alexander (Marie) of Dayton, Mrs. Ralph McSwain (Bessie) of California and Mrs. Cleda Rittenhouse of Sandusky.  Two sisters proceded her in death.   Services will 
2 CONC be at 11am Friday at the Jamieson Funeral Home, the Rev. Jogn Geissler officiating, burial will follow in the Miami Memorial Park in Covington.  Friends may call at the funeral home on Thursday from 5 to 8 pm.        Jamieson &amp
