2 ADDR
3 CITY Berlin
3 STAE NY
3 CTRY United States
1 DEAT
2 DATE 10 NOV 1906
2 PLAC Eldena, Lee County, Illinois, USA
2 ADDR
3 CTRY United States
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://cf.myheritageimages.com/records/dynamic/external/djvu/fbb/c92/2ab/_38c657bbc18b2e782f7c6714c99adab_0x0_.jpg?identifier=hakesfamily00byuhake&fs=www.myheritageimages.com&fspath=records%2FKC%2Fcompilation_of_p
2 CONC ublic_sources%2Fdjvu&page=133
2 CONT
2 CONT Children: Laura Elizebeth Burdick Clara Edith Burdick Estella Gertrude Paddock (born Burdick) Lula Mae Burdick Bessie Deot Burdick Elmer T. Burdick Loren E. Burdick Valdie A. Burdick Nettie A. Howard (born Burdick) Florence Hazel 
2 CONC Heinze (born Burdick) Emma Lillie Lambert (born Burdick) Ella Rosetta Burdick Dora G Sturtevant (born Burdick)
2 CONT MRS. THOMAS BURDICK OF ELDENA DEAD.
2 CONT
2 CONT Was an Early Settler of Lee County;
2 CONT Funeral Will be Held Monday.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mrs. Thomas Burdick died about 5 o'clock this morning at her home in Eldena from a complication of asthma and heart disease. She had been ailing for months, but her illness was not thought to be serious until this morning.
2 CONT She was born in New York state August 15, 1847, where she lived until 1886, at which time she removed to Illinois and was united in marriage to Thomas Burdick. During her life time Mrs. Burdick became the mother of thirteen childr
2 CONC en, two of whom died in infancy.
2 CONT
2 CONT Those left to mourn her death are Mrs. Edward (Nettie) Howard, Mrs. Wm. (Lulu) Paddock and Loren E. of Eldena; Mrs. John (Estella) Paddock, Mrs. John (Ella) Guptill, Valdie A., and Clara of this city;; Mrs. Dave (Emma) Lambert of 
2 CONC Nachusa township, Mrs. Frank (Laura) Rarick of Peoria and Elmer and Florence at home, and her husband (Thomas).
2 CONT Mrs. Burdick was one of Lee county's old settlers and was well known and highly respected by all the people in her neighborhood and has been a faithful wife and a good mother to her children, who are much bereaved for her apparent
2 CONC ly sudden demise.
2 CONT
2 CONT The funeral services will be held at the Evangelical church at Eldena at 10'oclock Monday morning and interment will be made in the Oakwood cemetery in Dixon.
2 CONT (Dixon Evening Telegraph, Dixon, IL., Sat., Nov. 10, 1906, pg. 5)* Reference: [https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/185016046/rosetta-sarah-burdick Find A Grave Memorial] - [https://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]:
