1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Twin sister of Ninnie Back.
2 CONT ----
2 CONT Annie Bell Back Ayres
2 CONT Birth
2 CONT 19 Jan 1874
2 CONT Morris County, Kansas, USA
2 CONT Death
2 CONT 23 Dec 1953 (aged 79)
2 CONT Platte County, Wyoming, USA
2 CONT Burial
2 CONT Douglas Park Cemetery
2 CONT Douglas, Converse County, Wyoming, USA
2 CONT Memorial ID
2 CONT 73391176 · View Source
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Annie Bell Back was born on January 19, 1874, in Morris County, Missouri; the daughter of Mr. and Mrs. Alexander Lee Back. She had a twin sister named Ninnie.
2 CONT
2 CONT Annie was united in marriage with Henry L. Spellman. on December 17, 1892, in Americus, Kanses. To this union, three daughters were born - Dollie, Minnie and Bertha.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1910, they moved from Kansas, to Kelso, Washington, residing there for four years, and then moving to Lost Springs, Wyoming, in 1914. There, they resided until the death of her husband. Following his death, Annie made her home 
2 CONC with her daughters, until she was united in marriage again, on September 23, 1947, with Ernest Ayres, of Glendo. They made their home on a ranch, east of Glendo, until the time of her death.
2 CONT
2 CONT She is survived by her husband, Ernest Ayres; three daughters, Mrs. Harry Watson of Fowler, Colorado; Mrs. Roy McCormick of Glendo; and Mrs. Louie Meinzer of Casper; one sister, Mrs. Mary Nix of Ranier, Oregon; seven grandchildren
2 CONC ; and six great-grandchildren. Two sisters and two brothers preceded her in death.
2 CONT
2 CONT Information was obtained from her obituary in the "Douglas Budget," December 31, 1953, and from cemetery records.
2 CONT Gravesite Details
2 CONT She is buried beside her first husband, Henry Spellman.
2 CONT
