1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Rachel Boggs Jones
2 CONT Birth
2 CONT Sep 1881
2 CONT Death
2 CONT 1919 (aged 37–38)
2 CONT Burial
2 CONT Morgan Cemetery
2 CONT Skyline, Letcher County, Kentucky, USA
2 CONT Memorial ID
2 CONT 97769359 · View Source
2 CONT Memorial
2 CONT Photos 2
2 CONT Flowers 1
2 CONT
2 CONT Added by Vonda
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Rachel Boggs' birth month and year (Sept. 1881) was taken from the 1900 Letcher County, KY, census. The 1910 Letcher County, KY, census indicates that she was born ca. 1883 (she was 27 years old). In the 1900 Letcher County, KY, c
2 CONC ensus, Rachel "Boggs" was listed as a "boarder" in the household of Joseph Jones' father and step-mother, John and Martha (Dorton) Jones, even though she was already married to Joseph Jones just two days earlier. Joseph and Rachel
2 CONC  were married on June 6, 1900, in Letcher County, KY, and they were enumerated in the 1900 Letcher County, KY, census on June 8, 1900.
2 CONT
2 CONT Rachel and Joseph had eight children: Manervia "Nerva" (Jones) Kimbley, Riley Jones, Nancy (Jones) Ison, Henry Jones, John D. Jones, Hettie Jones, Ada Jones and Patrick Jones.
2 CONT
2 CONT It was suspected that Rachel Boggs might be the daughter of Loranza and Polly Ann (Roark) Boggs (buried in this same cemetery) or Joseph and Manerva (Ingram) Boggs. However, after further review of census records and after speakin
2 CONC g with Lavene "Lee" Jones, grandson of Joseph and Rachel Jones, it appears that Rachel was most likely the daughter of Jesse Boggs and Elizabeth Caudill. Further research is needed to prove this connection. Rachel died sometime ju
2 CONC st before the 1920 Census was taken; Joseph was listed as being a widower.
2 CONT Gravesite Details
2 CONT No dates
