1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Named after his uncle Isaac William Wann, he was the son of [http://www.findagrave.com/cgi-bin/fg.cgi?page=gr&GSmid=46492489&GRid=24213114& David D. Franklin] & Mary Ann Wann.  He married [http://www.findagrave.com
2 CONC /cgi-bin/fg.cgi?page=gr&GSmid=46492489&GRid=24215590& Clara Thomason] on 1 Jan 1888, in Boone County, AR.  The marriage was blessed with eight children, including the oldest, [http://www.findagrave.com/cgi-bin/fg.cgi?page=gr&GSmid
2 CONC =46492489&GRid=7432500& Benjamin H], and [http://www.findagrave.com/cgi-bin/fg.cgi?page=gr&GSln=Cooksey&GScid=1729357&GRid=32326843& Laura Estella].
2 CONT
2 CONT Bill & Clara homesteaded 150 acres in Sycamore Hollow, near Alpena, Boone County, AR. in 1902.
2 CONT
2 CONT Clara died in 1908, and he remarried.  He had one child, David Leroy (b.1912), with his second wife.    
2 CONT
2 CONT He was living in Van Buren, AR when he died in 1918/19.
