1 NOTE {geni:about_me} married, son of Edwin S. Miller and Alice Knapp, husband of Florence Drury d. cert 60-004958 indicates a death date of March 6
2 CONT
2 CONT ------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Guy Miller of Trucking Firm Died At Brashear, Did Farm In Knox County
2 CONT
2 CONT Guy M. Miller of Brashear vicinity died at 1:30 o'clock Sunday morning, March 7, 1960. He had not been well for several months and confined to his home the last three weeks.
2 CONT
2 CONT Funeral services were Wednesday afternoon at the Easley Funeral Home in Brashear, conducted by the Rev. L. V. Hubbard, pastor of the Brashear Methodist Church. Burial was in the Sabbath Home Cemetery.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mr. Miller left his wife and a son, Gerald Miller, of Brashear and a foster daughter, Mrs. Donna Lee Person of Colorado; 2 grandsons; 2 granddaughters; a sister, Mrs. Atha Drury, of Kirksville. Mr. Miller was a son of Edwin S. and
2 CONC  Alice Knapp Miller, and he was married May 16, 1918, to Miss Florence Drury. They were the parents of one son, the one who survives.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mr. Miller was engaged in farming in Adair and Knox Counties until 1948 at which time he and his son formed the Miller & Son Trucking Company in Brashear.
2 CONT
2 CONT The Edina Sentinel Edina, Missouri March 10, 1960
