1 NOTE {geni:about_me} === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT Obituary - James T. Wolfe, 51, suffered a fatal heart attack Thursday morning at his home in Netawaka.  He was born December 28, 1907, in Virginia and spent most of his life in the Netawaka community.  He was a member of the Holto
2 CONC n Christian church.  He is survived by his wife, Mrs. Madeline Wolfe, of the home; a daughter, Mrs. Harold Larson, Holton; a son, Wendell Wolfe, Netawaka; three grandchildren; his mother, Mrs. Andrew Wolfe, Holton; eight sisters, 
2 CONC Mrs. Ben Hall, Mrs. Sherman Shupe, Mrs. Ralph McQueen, Mrs. Bertha Cramer, Mrs. Willis Moore and Mrs. William Bauer, all of Holton; Mrs. Melvin Coates, Netawaka and Mrs. Evan Ramsey, Wichita, and two brothers, Calvin Wolfe, Holton
2 CONC , and Harmon Wolfe, Hiawatha.  Burial will be at the Holton Cemetery.
