1 NOTE {geni:about_me} === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT Obituary - Belle M. Hall, 88, of Holton died Friday, April 6, 1990, at a Holton nursing home.  Mrs. Hall owned a catering service, a tea room and an antique shop for many years before she retired.  She was born July 5, 1901, in Le
2 CONC e County, VA, the daughter of Andrew and Elizabeth Edens Wolfe.  She lived in Holton for 35 years before she moved to Topeka in 1969.  She moved back to Holton in 1989.  Mrs. Hall was a member of Northland Christian Church, the Re
2 CONC scue Mission, the Senior Citizens Gage Bowling League, the Golden Diner Club, the Topeka Recreation Center and Garfield Golden Age Club, all in Topeka, and the Holton Hospital Auxiliary, the auxiliary of Mary L. Bair Post 44 of th
2 CONC e American Legion, the Holton Chamber of Commerce and Neighbors United, all in Holton.  She was a past president of the Holton Golden Age Club and a former member of the First Christian Church.  She was married to Benjamin Hall on
2 CONC  July 6, 1918.  He died May 23, 1965.  Survivors include a daughter, Virginia Crosswhite, Portland, OR; two sons, Ben J. Hall, Albany, MO and Larry Hall, Portland, OR; seven sisters, Bertha Jane Johnson and Mae Shupe, both of Tope
2 CONC ka, Lillie Jacobson, Hazel Moore and Fannie Brown, all of Holton, Myrtle Moore, Polk City, Iowa, and Lennie Coats, Netawaka; a brother Peter Wolfe, Hiawatha; 24 grandchildren; and many great-grandchildren.
