2 CONT Obituary - Mae V. Shupe, 88, Topeka, formerly of Holton, died Tuesday, Oct 8, 1991, at a Topeka retirement home.  Mrs. Shupe worked many years in the Central Service Department of Stormont Vail Hospital in Topeka. She was born Mar
2 CONC ch 26, 1903, at Hagan, VA, the daughter of Andrew H. and Sarah Elizabeth Edens Wolfe.  She lived in Topeka since 1980 and formerly spent most of her life in the Holton and Netawaka communities.  Mrs. Shupe was a member of Gage Chr
2 CONC istian Church in Topeka and a former member of First Christian Church in Holton, KS.  She was married to Sherman Shupe Sept 7, 1919, at Whiting.  He died April 25, 1979.  Survivors include three daughters, Gladys Shay, Kansas City
2 CONC , KS, Ivone Miller, Dallas, TX and Shirley Ann Clowe, Salem, IL; six sisters, Lillie Jacobson, Bertha Johnson, Hazel Moore and Fannie Brown, all of Holton, Lennie Coates, Netawaka, and Myrtle Moore, Polk City, Iowa; a brother, Har
2 CONC mon "Pete" Wolfe, Hiawatha; eight grandchildren; eight great-grandchildren and a great-great-grandchild.
