2 CONT * '''Residence''': 1910 - Moccasin, Russell, Virginia, United States
2 CONT * '''Residence''': 1920 - Moccasin Magisterial District, Russell, Virginia, United States
2 CONT ** Reference: [https://www.myheritage.com/research/record-40001-832695046/nancy-c-wolfe-born-lasley-in-familysearch-family-tree FamilySearch Family Tree] - [https://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Jan 25 2026, 
2 CONC 1:06:47 UTC''
2 CONT
2 CONT Nancy Lasley grew up on a farm in Russell County, Virginia. She was the fifth of eleven children born to Robert and Mary Ward Lasley.  Her mother Mary, known locally as "Granny Lasley" was an unusual person. She was half Cherokee 
2 CONC and worked with herbs to help those who were sick.  Granny Lasley must have passed some of her healing skills on to her daughter, because later in life, Nancy acted as a midwife.  At about age 16, she married Zeno Wolfe, a former 
2 CONC confederate soldier.  The couple lived on a farm and went on to have five children: James, William Walter, Mattie, Josie A. and Ada Francis.  Life was not easy after about 1900 when Zeno was forced to apply for a soldier's disabil
2 CONC ity pension due to rheumatism and other problems. Nancy helped out at this time, even bringing in extra income to the family through her work as a midwife.  Nancy died in 1930, but not before telling my grandmother about her life.
2 CONC  My grandmother told me, and that is how I know of her heritage, a story I am passing on here.* Reference: [https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/67134182/nancy-wolfe Find A Grave Memorial] - [https://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy
2 CONC /18783 SmartCopy]: ''Jan 25 2026, 1:12:36 UTC''
