1 SUBM @S6000000020342989284@
1 OBJE
2 FILE https://www.geni.com/images/documents/doc.png
2 FORM txt
2 TITL Peacock Web Site
1 NOTE !     In the book, HISTORY OF THE HARBOR DISTRICT OF LOS ANGELES by
2 CONT Ella A. Ludwig, this biography of John Franklin Dollins is found on page
2 CONT 409-11.
2 CONT
2 CONT !     A scion of old and prominent families of the Blue Grass state, John F.
2 CONT Dollins lived for many years in the south, witnessing its devastation and
2 CONT reconstruction.  He contributed his quota toward the upbuilding and
2 CONT progress of that region and now exerts a strong and beneficial influence
2 CONT in business circles of San Pedro through his activities as a restaurateur.
2 CONT !     He was born June 9, l854, in Stanford, Lincoln county, Kentucky, and
2 CONT is the oldest son and child of Benjamin Franklin and Sarah F. (Marshall)
2 CONT Dollins, both of whom were born in that state.  The Dollins family is of
2 CONT Welsh origin, and in the maternal line he is descended from illustrious
2 CONT Virginians.  His mother was a niece of General Humphrey Marshall, who
2 CONT achieved distinction in the Mexican war, and she was also closely
2 CONT related to the eminent jurist, John Marshall, who served as Chief Justice
2 CONT of the Supreme Court of the United States from 180l until 1835.
2 CONT Benjamin F. Dollins developed two large, productive farms and aided in
2 CONT raising the standards of fruit growing in Kentucky, which numbered him
2 CONT among its pioneer ochardists.  He was a man of varied interests and the
2 CONT first registered distiller in the mountain district of Pulaski county. Endowed
2 CONT with exeptional business acumen and foresight, he prospered in
2 CONT all of his undertakings, and his integrity was above question.  He was a
2 CONT stanch supporter of the Union cause and greatly admired Abraham
2 CONT Lincoln.  He attained the ripe age of eighty-five, and his wife reached the
2 CONT ninety-first milestone on life's journey.   To their union were born three
2 CONT children: John F.;  Charles Marshall, who was a prominent merchant of
2 CONT Greenville, Texas and there passed away in l927, when sixty-seven years of
2 CONT age; and Mollie, a resident of Somerset, Kentucky and the widow of Dr.
2 CONT Huddle, who practiced for a number of years at Paris, Texas.
2 CONT !     John F. Dollins was reared on the homestead and had limited educational
2 CONT advantages, attending the district school only three months
2 CONT of the year.  This was during the winter season, and in the meantime he
2 CONT assisted his father in tilling the soil and caring for the crops.  The farm
2 CONT was located near the scene of a bitter contest between the Federal and
2 CONT Confederate troops, and on the morning after the contest he visited the
2 CONT Mills Spring battlefield, which was strewn with many dead bodies,
2 CONT including those of General Zollikoffer and Lieutenant Peyton.  Mr. Dollins
2 CONT was then a boy of ten,  and the tragic event left an ineffaceable impression
2 CONT upon his mind.
2 CONT !     When a young man of twenty-one Mr. Dollins started out in life for
2 CONT himself.  After his first marriage he took his bride to Somerset,
2 CONT Kentucky.  The line of the Cincinnati Southern, now known as the Cincinnati,
2 CONT New Orleans and Texas Pacific Railroad, was then being extended through
2 CONT that section, and he aided in grading the road bed, later working in the
2 CONT railroad shops.  Subsequently he was a locomotive
2 CONT fireman on that line and for three years his run was from Somerset to
2 CONT Cincinnati and Chattanooga.  In l888 he went to Wichita Falls, Texas and
2 CONT in l889 moved to Fort Worth, that state, where he made him home for
2 CONT thirty-five years.  During seven years of that period he was a member of
2 CONT the police force and afterward engaged in teaming and hauling on a large
2 CONT scale and also becoming a cotton buyer for the Planters Compress
2 CONT Company.  Mr. Dollins witnessed the growth of Fort Worth from forty
2 CONT thousand to a population of one hundred and forty thousand, and his
2 CONT progress paralleled that of the city.  In l923 he came to California,
2 CONT bringing with him considerable means accumulated by years of hard work
2 CONT and good management, and in l927 opened "Dad's Place," situated at No.
2 CONT 909 South Seaside Avenue on Terminal Island in East San Pedro.  This is
2 CONT one of the most attractive and inviting cafes in the Harbor District and
2 CONT draws its patrons from all walks of life.  The place is scrupulously
2 CONT clean, and the food is tempting and appetizing.  The coffee is
2 CONT particularly good, and the service is first class in every particular.
2 CONT !     In Richmond, Kentucky, Mr. Dollins was married July 30, l875 to Miss
2 CONT Sarah F. Vaught, who was a native of Somerset, Kentucky, and of German
2 CONT lineage.  Mrs. Dollins died at Fort Worth in l893,  [Sarah's true date of
2 CONT death is Jan. 24, l923, this stated date of l893 is incorrect-per Carol D.
2 CONT Crabtree Peacock, her great grandaughter]   leaving a family of four
2 CONT children: Charles Carl, who is a deputy sheriff of Los Angeles county and
2 CONT proprietor of the Radio Restaurant at East San Pedro; Birdie, who is the
2 CONT wife of Earl Robertson, of Kansas City, Missouri; Ben Logan,(note: Carol D.
2 CONT Crabtree Peacock's grandfather)  the proprietor of a bakery in Fort Worth,
2 CONT Texas and Edward, who for ten years has been connected with the fire
2 CONT department of that city.
2 CONT At Clayton, Missouri, Mr. Dollins was married in l924 to Mrs. Charles Parker,
2 CONT a widow, who bore the maiden name of Katherine Hargis and was born in
2 CONT Somerset, Kentucky.  By her first union she became the mother of a
2 CONT daughter, who is now Mrs. Sophia Evans and resides in Somerset.  Mrs.
2 CONT Dollins assists her husband in the cafe and works untiringly for the success
2 CONT of the business. She adheres to the Presbyterian faith and
2 CONT closely follows the teachings of the church.
2 CONT !     Mr. Dollins casts his ballot for the candidates of the republican
2 CONT party, and his fraternal connections are with the Eagles, the Knights of
2 CONT Pythias and the Woodmen of the World.  He is well informed regarding all
2 CONT matters of public moment and heartily cooperates in movements for the
2 CONT general good.  He has wisely conserved his powers, and at the age of
2 CONT seventy-three is vigorous in mind and body.  He possesses a retentive
2 CONT memory and keen powers of observation, and his conversation spans the
2 CONT past in interesting reminiscences.  The Golden Rule has constituted his
2 CONT guide throughtout life, and a frank, sympathetic and genial nature has
2 CONT drawn to him a host of steadfast friends.
2 CONT
2 CONT John F. Dollins is buried in Greenwood Cemetery in Section 3 E Space 3.
1 SOUR
2 DATA
3 DATE 20 NOV 2025
3 TEXT Date of Birth
3 TEXT
1 SOUR
