1 NOTE !     Charles C. was in the Spanish American War. his grandaughter, Euella
2 CONT Rogers said he was a longshoreman in California.  In a note received from
2 CONT Euella that was written by her Dad, Bert Carl, it states that  his Dad's
2 CONT birthdate was 2 Feb 1879 and he died in Fall of 1940.  Found in Star
2 CONT Telegram newspaper, his obit.  He died on Sept. l9, l940 and was buried
2 CONT on Sept. 21, l940 in Greenwood Cemetery in the John F. Dollins Plot.
2 CONT
2 CONT !     In the book HISTORY OF THE HARBOR DISTRICT OF LOS ANGELES by Ella
2 CONT A. Ludwig, this biography of Charles Carl Dollins is found on page  835.
2 CONT !     Charles Carl Dollins, who typifies the spirit of progress in East San
2 CONT Pedro, has achieved success in the restaurant business and also figures
2 CONT conspicuously in public affairs, ably discharging the duties of a deputy
2 CONT sheriff.  A native of Kentucky, he was born May l, l876, in Somerset and
2 CONT is the oldest of the four children of John F. and Sarah F. (Vaught) Dollins,
2 CONT the latter of whom is deceased.  The father is the genial proprietor of
2 CONT "Dad's Place," one of the leading cafes of East San Pedro, and a detailed
2 CONT account of his life is published elsewhere in this volume.
2 CONT !     During his boyhood Charles C. Dollins lived at home with his parents, and
2 CONT his education was completed in the public schools of Wichita Falls
2 CONT and Fort Worth, Texas.  In the latter city his parents settled in l889,
2 CONT when he was thirteen years of age.  There he was reared to manhhod and
2 CONT for four years was one of the Texas Rangers.  At San Antonio, Texas, he
2 CONT reenlisted in l898 for service in the Spanish-American war and
2 CONT afterward was sent to the Philippines with Compnay H of the Second
2 CONT Texas Infantry.  After receiving his honorable discharge Mr. Dollins
2 CONT returned to Fort Worth, where he was engaged in business until l907,
2 CONT when he went to Missouri, and for five years conducted a rooming house
2 CONT in Kansas City.  He spent six years in Akron, Ohio, and in l9l8 came to
2 CONT California, locating in San Pedro, where he has since made his home.  In
2 CONT l922 he opened the Radio Restaurant, which is situated at No. 79l South
2 CONT Seaside Avenue on Terminal Island in East San Pedro, and is regarded as
2 CONT one of the best eating places in the town.  The service is adapted to
2 CONT every need and a large and constantly incresasing clientele is indicative
2 CONT of the prestige of the cafe.  Mr. Dollins has a economic knowlege of modern
2 CONT food values and closely supervises every detail of the business, working
2 CONT from four-thirty in the morning until seven o'clock at night, and
2 CONT is ably assisted by Mrs. Dollins and a number of trained employees and
2 CONT cooks.
2 CONT !     In 1899 Mr. Dollins was married in Fort Worth, Texas, to Miss Minnie
2 CONT Cooper, now deceased, who was the mother of three children: Henry, who
2 CONT conducts a garage in Fort Worth, Texas;  Bert Carl, who is employed by
2 CONT the Crescent Wharf & Warehouse Company of San Pedro; and Charles, who
2 CONT is connected with an  automobile finance company of Fort Worth.  Mr.
2 CONT Dollins was married August 22, l9l5, in Buffalo, New York, to Miss Edith
2 CONT Tanner, who was born and reared in Greenville, Texas and ably assists
2 CONT her husband in managing the business.  They have an attractive home at
2 CONT No. 672 West Twenty-first Street in San Pedro and are consistent
2 CONT members of the Methodist Episcopal church.
2 CONT !     Mr. Dollins has been identified with the Loyal Order of Moose for a
2 CONT period of twenty years and takes a keen interest in its activities.  His
2 CONT military training and experience well qualify him for the responsible
2 CONT position of deputy sheriff of Los Angeles county, to which he was appointed
2 CONT by Sheriff W.E. Traeger in l926, and his work has been highly satisfactory.
2 CONT He visions a great future for the harbor district and is a "live wire" in his
2 CONT community.  He has never deviated form the course dictated by conscience
2 CONT and honor, and the respect accorded him is well deserved.
