1 NOTE {geni:about_me} FUNERAL OF WILLIAM H. ZIKE
2 CONT
2 CONT Funeral services for William H. Zike, McMillan quarry workman who lost his life Thursday in a plunge over a ledge at Reed's Station, was today at two o'clock from the Harrodsburg Methodist Church and interment in the cemetery ther
2 CONC e beside the body of his wife.
2 CONT
2 CONT [http://www.findagrave.com/cgi-bin/fg.cgi?page=gr&GRid=23115418 Pauline], daughter of Mr. Zike, arrived in Bedford from Bloomington Thursday afternoon and made the funeral arrangements.  The remains were taken from the funeral hom
2 CONC e late Thursday to the home of the deceased's sister, [http://www.findagrave.com/cgi-bin/fg.cgi?page=gr&GRid=19313463 Mrs. John M. Walls], where they lie in state until the remains were removed to Harrodsburg for the funeral.
2 CONT
2 CONT Bloomington Daily Telephone,  September 5, 1925,  Clipping File,  Monroe County History Center,  Bloomington, Indiana.
2 CONT -----------------------
2 CONT William & [http://www.findagrave.com/cgi-bin/fg.cgi?page=gr&GRid=19313169 Della] had atleast 3 children: [http://www.findagrave.com/cgi-bin/fg.cgi?page=gr&GRid=19313211 Lewis], [http://www.findagrave.com/cgi-bin/fg.cgi?page=gr&GRi
2 CONC d=19313627 Fletcher] & [http://www.findagrave.com/cgi-bin/fg.cgi?page=gr&GRid=23115418 Pauline]. Note: (#1723)
