2 CONT
2 CONT Robert Lee Alexander  -  Military Service During WWII    
2 CONT Dates                  Events 
2 CONT June 6 1939  Enlisted in the Ohio National Guard  
2 CONT 15 October, 1940  Ohio National Guard Federalized  
2 CONT October, 1942  OH National Guard to Camp Shelby, Missisippi for training  
2 CONT January, 1942  Promoted to Corperal  
2 CONT April, 1942  Promoted to Sergeant Company "M" 148th Infantry  
2 CONT May, 1942  Left by ship for Pacific Theater  
2 CONT July, 1942  First letter from home arrived  
2 CONT September, 1942   Second letter arrived  
2 CONT July, 1943  Battle of Munda on New Georgia Island  
2 CONT October 27, 1943  Awarded Combat Infantry Badge  
2 CONT November, 1943  Battle of Bouganville  
2 CONT December, 1943  Promoted to Staff Sergeant  
2 CONT February, 1944  Promoted to Tech Sergeant  
2 CONT January, 1945  Battle of Phillipines  
2 CONT February 5. 1945  Wounded in the battle of Manila  
2 CONT February 5, 1945  Moved to 54th Evacuation Hospital  
2 CONT March 1, 1945  Casualty telegram sent to mother by War Department  
2 CONT March 12, 1945  Moved to 105th Hospital  
2 CONT April 1, 1945  Sent by air ambulance to San Fransico  
2 CONT April4, 1945  Sent to General Hospital, Fort Benjamin Harrison, Indiana  
2 CONT June 15, 1945  Discharged from Arm Service  
2 CONT October 12, 1947  Received WWII Victory Medal &amp; American Defense Medal   
2 CONT by mail at 266 1/2 Obell Ct. Dayton, Ohio  
2 CONT
2 CONT Army Service 4 years and 8 months    
2 CONT Overseas service 35 months    
2 CONT
2 CONT Medals &amp; Ribbons    
2 CONT Combat Infantry Badge, Asiatic Pacific Theater Ribbon with 4 Bronze Stars,    
2 CONT Philippine Liberation Ribbon with one bronze star, Purple Heart,    
2 CONT American Defense Ribbon, Good Conduct Metal    
2 CONT Weapons Badges: Rifle Expert, Carbine Expert, Heavy Machinegun Expert.
