1 NOTE BIOGRAPHY: Diary Reference.
2 CONT Letter. CH Baker to CW Baker in 1902.
2 CONT C.M. Young Diary. Several references. Specifically, Files # 214,215&216
2 CONT Jan 1, 1889 "Everet & Roscoe Baker'.
2 CONT BIRTH: Birth does not show in 1880 Census. Diary references in 1885-1900
2 CONT timeframe mention Roscoe. 1902 letter from C.H.Baker to C. W. Baker
2 CONT mentions Roscoe. 1890 Census was destroyed so Roscoe doesn't show up.
2 CONT By 1900, he was 19 to 20 years old and probably out of the house. He
2 CONT doesn't show up in the C. H. Basker family in Lousiville, Ky. Search to date
2 CONT has not ocated Roscoe after time of last diary reference.
