1 FAMC @F6000000005234821000@
1 FAMS @F6000000005234813569@
1 RFN geni:6000000005234588397
1 SUBM @S6000000005234123779@
1 NOTE Information from Carol Doyle email on February 10, 2006:
2 CONT
2 CONT Myrtle Etta Mae Clark born Feb 25, 1902 in Joplin, Newton County, Missouri, daughter of Charles Monroe and Isabelle "Belle" (Baugh) Clark.  She moved with her parents to Terryville, SD (near Lead, South Dakota ) to homestead, atte
2 CONC nded school there until she came to Chadron State Teachers College in 1923 where she received her teaching certificate.  She married Lester E. Wilkins Tagart on June 14, 1923 in Chadron, Nebraska.  Lester was born January 19, 1903
2 CONC  in Vesta, Johnson County, Nebraska sone of James and Ida W (Starling) Tagart who were married July 13, 1893.  Lester came with his parents and sibling to Crawford in 1917 and farmed east of Crawford.  Myrtle died March 25, 1973 a
2 CONC nd Lester died January 4, 1989.  Myrtle taught at District 84 Hardscrabble School (where your grandmother taught and where Jim, Kenny and Nancy attended school)  in 1927/28, 1928/29 and 1929/30.
2 CONT
2 CONT This is from the book "History of Hardscrabble School 1887-2000, District 84 located in Dawes  County Nebraska" published by myself and Gerald A. Miller.  Gerald is quite a genealogist and obtained information such as the above fo
2 CONC r all but a couple of the teachers of those 113 years. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Myrtle had a brother Homer (Jack) who married my cousin Isabelle Lange. They divorced after 40 years!  He also had a brother Jess and I think maybe another sister.
2 CONT Jack is buried in Chadron cemetery and Jess was from Washington (?) and had a boy and girl as I remember.
