2 ADDR
1 DEAT
2 DATE 12 AUG 1971
2 PLAC Saint Joseph, Buchanan County, Missouri, USA
2 ADDR
1 OCCU
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Chester Smith, of 21, and Ellenor Miller, over 18, were married March 13, 1936 at Maysville.  (Source: DeKalb County, MO Marriage Records)
2 CONT ===============================================
2 CONT
2 CONT St. Joseph Gazette (St. Joseph, MO), Friday, August 13, 1971; pg. 3
2 CONT
2 CONT Mrs. Ellenor Elizabeth Smith, 52, the wife of Benjamin Chester Smith, of 2022 Jules, died Thursday morning in a St. Joseph hospital.  
2 CONT
2 CONT Mrs. Smith was an employe (sic) for the Missouri Methodist Hospital.  She was born in Stanberry, Mo.
2 CONT
2 CONT Survivors, besides her husband of the home, include a son, Kenneth Smith of King City, Mo.; two daughters, Mrs. Caroline Lipe of Wathena, Kan., and Mrs. Shirley Deen of Albany, Mo.; four sisters, Mrs. Annabelle Yount of King City,
2 CONC  Mrs. Byrdene Martin and Mrs. Vonda Frizzell, both of Kansas City, Mo., and Mrs. Ruth Guidice of New York, N.Y., and six grandchildren.
2 CONT
2 CONT Services will be at 2 p.m. Saturday in the Clark mortuary at King City.  The Rev. Martin Barker will officiate with burial in the King City cemetery (sic).
2 CONT ======================================================
2 CONT
2 CONT Tri-County News (King City, MO), Friday, August 20, 1971; pg. 5
2 CONT
2 CONT The funeral of Mrs. Ellenor Elizabeth Smith was held Saturday at the Clark Funeral Home here, conducted by the Rev. Martin Barker.  Burial was in the King City cemetery (sic).  Mrs. Smith, an employe (sic) at the Methodist hospita
2 CONC l in St. Joseph, was born in Stanberry and is a former resident of King City.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mrs. Gerald Johnson and Mrs. B.G. Clark sang "Beyond the Sunset" and "Just a Closer Walk with Thee," accompanied by Mrs. Lee Pulley, organist.  Pallbearers were Jimmy Holt, Roger Smith, John Jacobs, Michael Smith, Larry Parker, Da
2 CONC le Wright.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mrs. Smith was born near Island City and spent her entire life in this area.  On Feb. 13, 1936, she married Benjamin Smith and they were parents of 3 children.
2 CONT
2 CONT Survivors include her husband of the home, 1 son Kenneth Smith of King City; 2 daughters, Mrs. Caroline Lipe of Wathena, Kas., and Mrs. Shirley Deen of Albany; 4 sisters, Mrs. Annabelle Yount of King City, Mrs. Byrdene Martin and 
2 CONC Mrs. Vanda Frizzell of Kansas City, and Mrs. Ruth Guidice of New York, N.Y., and 6 grandchildren.* Reference: [https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/136524929/ellenor-elizabeth-smith Find A Grave Memorial] - [https://www.geni.com/pr
