1 NOTE {geni:about_me} m: Mrs. Lucy Plymale 29 Oct 1934 in Maryville, Nodaway Co, MO
2 CONT
2 CONT John Frederick Motzkus, 89, of Okanogan, died Sunday, Nov. 29, 1998, at a Spokane hospital.
2 CONT
2 CONT He moved to Wenatchee in the mid-1930s, and worked as a carpenter and in the fruit industry. He later moved near Mazama, where he farmed and worked in sawmills. He returned to Wenatchee in 1962, where he owned and operated orchard
2 CONC s and managed an orchard for Lee Stout for many years.
2 CONT
2 CONT Survivors include daughters, Mary Ann Bame of Twisp, and Betty Hubler of Aberdeen; and a son, Gary Plymale of Wenatchee.
2 CONT
2 CONT Funeral services will be held at 1 p.m. Saturday at Calvary Baptist Church in Twisp, the Rev. John Smith officiating.
2 CONT
2 CONT Visitation will be held from 10 a.m. to noon Saturday at Precht's Methow Valley Chapel.
2 CONT
2 CONT Arrangements are by Precht's Methow Valley Chapel.
