1 NOTE {geni:about_me} * Reference: [https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/96449010/paulina-lena-wencl Find A Grave Memorial] - [https://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Apr 12 2023, 5:28:32 UTC''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT Final tribute was paid Mrs. Louis Wencl, 76, when her funeral services were held here Monday. Mrs. Wencl, ill for over a year, died at her home Friday morning. Services were held at Sacred Heart church, the Rev. Urban Neudecker si
2 CONC nging the Requiem Mass at 10 o'clock. Interment followed in Sacred Heart cemetery. The daughter of the late Mr. and Mrs. Anton Kubat, Mrs. Wencl was born and raised in Steele county, acquiring during that time a host of friends wh
2 CONC o mourn her death. She was born September 16, 1869. Surviving are her husband and two sons, Louis and William, Owatonna, and three daughters, Mrs. George (Agnes) Pichner, Mrs. R. C. (Alice) Jirikowic, and Miss Mary Wencl, at home.
2 CONC  Also surviving are seven grandchildren, and one great grandchild. One grandson, Lawrence Niclawske, is serving with the U. S. Navy at Pearl Harbor, and one grandson died in a German prison camp. There are also seven brothers surv
2 CONC iving, Joseph and Vincent of Owatonna, Emil, Henry, John and William of Mora, Minnesota and Edward of Fargo, North Dakota. Four brothers and a sister preceded her in death.
