1 NOTE {geni:about_me} http://findagrave.com/cgi-bin/fg.cgi?page=gr&GSln=Stransky&GSfn=Joseph+&GSmn=M.&GSiman=1&GSbyrel=all&GSdyrel=all&GSob=n&GRid=106117343&df=all&
2 CONT
2 CONT Birth: 	Jan. 30, 1881 Minnesota, USA Death: 	Nov. 23, 1954 Milwaukie Clackamas County Oregon, USA
2 CONT
2 CONT MILWAUKIE (Special) – Service was Friday in Oregon City for Joseph M. Stransky, prominent Milwaukie area businessman, who died Tuesday in a Portland hospital. Officers of the Musicians local conducted the rites in Hillsdale chapel
2 CONC . Burial was in Riverview Abbey mausoleum.
2 CONT
2 CONT Deceased was born January 30, 1881, in Minnesota. He had lived in the Milwaukie-Portland area about 32 years. He founded the Stransky Lumber company at Wichita, a Milwaukie suburb, November 11, 1929, 1nd was active in its manageme
2 CONC nt until a few days before his death.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mr. Stransky was a member of the Veterans of Foreign Wars, Musicians Post 185, of which he was a past commander, Milwaukie AF&AM Masonic lodge, American Skokol association and Musicians Mutual association. He played baritone horn 
2 CONC in several bands, including the Portland Elks, Letter Carriers' and Musicians.
2 CONT
2 CONT Survivors include the widow, Mabel; two daughters, Mrs. Mildred Judd of Oswego and Miss Ardice Stransky of Portland; two sons, Waldo of Portland and Malcolm of Redwood City, Cal., three brothers and a sister in Minnesota, and four
2 CONC  grandchildren.
2 CONT
2 CONT [The Oregonian, 27 Nov 1954, p11] 
2 CONT
