1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Rome Sentinel
2 CONT March 24, 1908
2 CONT
2 CONT Jonathan B. Hakes, one of the oldest and most respected residents of Dix, died at the Rome Hospital at 5 o'clock on Monday afternoon, having been taken there 10 days ago suffering from Bright's disease.  It was known that his case
2 CONC  was hopeless but he was admitted that his last days be passed as comfortably as possible.  Mr. Hakes was born in Berlin, Renesselaer county 73 years ago, and when about 20 years old he went to Dix where he had since lived, follow
2 CONC ing the occupation of a farmer.  Mr. Hakes was twice married, his second wife dying five years ago.  His survived by two daughters, Miss Roselin Hakes, who lives and home, and Mrs. J. W. McPherson of Canastota.* Reference: [https:
2 CONC //www.findagrave.com/memorial/11660837/jonathan-b-hakes Find A Grave Memorial] - [https://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Dec 1 2021, 5:35:55 UTC''
