1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Henry Louis Spellman
2 CONT Birth
2 CONT 8 Jan 1864
2 CONT Bloomington, McLean County, Illinois, USA
2 CONT Death
2 CONT 6 Jun 1938 (aged 74)
2 CONT Shawnee, Converse County, Wyoming, USA
2 CONT Burial
2 CONT Douglas Park Cemetery
2 CONT Douglas, Converse County, Wyoming, USA
2 CONT Memorial ID
2 CONT 70076029 · View Source
2 CONT
2 CONT Henry Louis Spellman was born January 8, 1864 in Bloomington, Illinois; the son of Mr. and Mrs. Thomas Spellman. During his early years they moved from Illinois to Kansas, where he grew to manhood, and where at Americus, he marrie
2 CONC d Annie Bell Back on December 17, 1892.
2 CONT
2 CONT To them were born three daughters, Dolly, Minnie and Bertha. In 1910 they moved from Kansas to Kelso, Washington, residing there four years, then coming to Lost Springs, Wyoming in 1914, where they lived on their homestead until 1
2 CONC 932.
2 CONT
2 CONT He suffered his first stroke April 13, 1933, after which they moved to Douglas; and from Douglas on January 1, 1937 to the home of their daughter, Mrs. Bertha Pickinpaugh, near Orin. In August, 1937 they made their home in Shawnee
2 CONC . He had been bedfast most of the time for the last 13 months of his life.
2 CONT
2 CONT Survivors were his widow, Mrs. Annie Spellman; and three daughters, Mrs. Louis Meinzer and Mrs. Bertha Pickenpaugh, both of Shawnee; and Mrs. Archie Baker of Glendo, Wyoming; one brother residing at Emporia, Kansas; five grandchil
2 CONC dren and numerous other relatives.
2 CONT
2 CONT Two brothers, George and Don, preceded him in death.
2 CONT
2 CONT Information was obtained from his obituary.
2 CONT Family Members
2 CONT Parents
2 CONT
2 CONT Thomas H Spellman
2 CONT 1812–1883
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Caroline E. Day Lamb
2 CONT 1834–1910
2 CONT
