1 NAME Wendell Gerald /Bach/
2 GIVN Wendell Gerald
2 _MARNM Bach
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE 1921
1 DEAT
2 DATE 2005
1 OCCU
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Wendell Gerald Bach, 83, of 28 Hillcrest Drive, husband of Ima Jane Wood Bach for 46 years, died at 2:35 p.m. Saturday at Select Speciality Hospital, Lexington.
2 CONT
2 CONT A native of Rousseau, Breathitt County, he was the son of the late Melvin Bach and the late Visa Risner Bach Jones. He was a retired employee of the Lexington Bluegrass Army Depot, a member of Central Baptist Church, an Army veter
2 CONC an of World War II, a Mason. and a 1970 Kentucky Colonel.
2 CONT
2 CONT Additional survivors include two daughters and a son-in-law, Susan Ragland, Lexington, and Linda and Steve Epley, Maysville, N.C.; two sons and daughters-in-law, Timothy Glyn and Jacque Bach, Winchester, and Cecil Ray and Cody Bac
2 CONC h, Indiana Harbor, Fla.; a stepson and daughter-in-law, William E. and Patty Butler, Mt. Sterling; nine grandchildren, Andrew Bach, Lauren Bach, Wendi Boykin, Mike Ragland, Jay Ragland, Chris Bach, Cindy Robards, Mike Butler and M
2 CONC ark Butler; 10 great-grandchildren, a brother, Charles Paul Bach, North Carolina; a sister, Geneva Couch, Leesburg, Fla., and a sister-in-law, JoAnn Miller, Winchester.
2 CONT
2 CONT Services will be conducted at 1 p.m. Wednesday at Scobee Funeral Home by Rev. Cova Duvall and Dr. Art Beasley. Burial will be in the Winchester Cemetery.
2 CONT
2 CONT Pallbearers will be Andrew Bach, Mike Ragland, Mike Butler, Bill Couch, Mike Sallee, Donnie Miller, Chris Bach, Jay Ragland, Wendi Boykin, Lauren Bach and Mark Butler; honorary, R.B. and Lila Omohundro, Otis Henry, Otis Curtis, Ch
2 CONC arlie Birch, Kerney Hill, James Owens, Kenneth Armitage, Linda Anes, Roxie Hash, Sharon Dixon, Dr. Thomas Burchett,
2 CONT Marion Baber, Kenny Lear and the staff and physicians of elect Speciality Hospital, Lexington.
2 CONT
2 CONT Friends may call 6-8 p.m. today.
2 CONT
2 CONT Memorials may take the form of contributions to the American Cancer Society, c/o Woodie Wills, 43 Mahan Drive, Winchester, Ky. 40391
