1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Nora Cecil (Dixon) Asher was the daughter of James C. and Evelyn "Eva" (Back) Dixon.  She married Curtis Asher on September 5, 1926.  They had three children: William Curtis Asher, Anita Jean (Asher) Campbell and M
2 CONC ary Kathryn "Kay" (Asher) Tandy.
2 CONT
2 CONT - - - - - -
2 CONT
2 CONT The obituary of Nora (Dixon) Asher as published in the February 24, 1993, issue of The Mountain Eagle:
2 CONT
2 CONT Former Letcher postmaster dies
2 CONT
2 CONT Nora Dixon Asher, 88, of Lexington, died February 22 in Lexington.
2 CONT
2 CONT A daughter of the late James and Evelyn Back Dixon, she was the widow of Curtis Asher.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mrs. Asher was a retired postmaster from the Letcher Post Office.
2 CONT
2 CONT Surviving are a son, William Curtis Asher, Letcher; two daughters, Anita Campbell, Lexington; Kathryn Kaye, Denver, Colo.; two sisters, Rebecca Warner and Lillian Monhollin, both of Crittenden; five grandchildren, and four great-g
2 CONC randchildren.
2 CONT
2 CONT Funeral services were to be held February 23 at Pruitt's Funeral Home in Lexington.
2 CONT
2 CONT A graveside service will be held today (Wednesday) at 1 p.m. at the Dixon Cemetery at Elk Creek.
