1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Lily Eldridge Newman, 80, widow of Robert Stephen Newman passed away on Tuesday, May 28, 2024 Pikeville Medical Center.  She was born on July 21, 1943 in Blackey, Kentucky to the late Crit Eldridge and Susie Caudil
2 CONC l Eldridge. She was retired from Fort Boonesborough State Park where she was a manager. Lily took great pride in her heritage in Eastern Kentucky as well as her grandchildren, whom she loved dearly. She was a member of Friendship 
2 CONC Old Regular Baptist Church. 
2 CONT
2 CONT She is survived by three sons, Donnie Newman (Jennifer), Steve Newman (Awndrea) and Jim Newman (Sheila), all of Richmond, Kentucky; one daughter, Melissa Ballinger (Tobey) of Richmond, Kentucky; eleven grandchildren and twelve gre
2 CONC at grandchildren. 
2 CONT
2 CONT In addition to her husband and parents, she is preceded in passing by all of her siblings. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Services will be held on Monday, June 3, 2024 at 1:00 p.m. at Oldham, Roberts and Powell Funeral Home with James Hardin and Chip Deneif officiating. Visitation will be from 11:00 a.m. until the time of service.
2 CONT
2 CONT Pallbearers will be Austin Newman, Joey Ohler, Rob Newman, Tanner Hembree, Jon Lainhart and Mike Hoover. Honorary pallbearers will be J.C. Blair, Richard Blair, Bill Hendricks, Doug Townsend, Renee Allen, Millie Leach, Carl Hoover
2 CONC , John Childers, Betty Eldridge, Harlin Eldridge and Jeanie Dunaway. 
