1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Carson Euell Sumner, age 85, passed away on Wednesday, April 24, 2024, at Saint Joseph Hospital in Lexington, Kentucky. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He was born in Rosslyn, Kentucky, on October 5, 1938, to the late Bryan Sumner and the late Helen Wilson Sumner. Euell was a lifelong farmer who raised corn, tobacco, and livestock. He loved to hunt and fish. Euell loved Chevrolet
2 CONC  cars. He had a high level of integrity and was a lifelong learner. Euell served in the United States Army and was proud to have served his country. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Mr. Sumner is survived by his wife, Margie Sumner of Stanton; one daughter, Angela Chapman (Glenn) of Stanton; one grandchild, Taylor Chapman Blevins (Zachary); and three great grandchildren, Harper Kate Blevins, Adalynn Marie Ble
2 CONC vins, and Porter Reece Blevins. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Visitation was held from 1-3 p.m. on Friday, April 26, 2024, at Hearne Funeral Home, 125 West College Avenue, Stanton, Kentucky. Funeral services officiated by Bro. Wesley Miller were held at the funeral home immediately following
2 CONC  the visitation at 3 p.m. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Burial was at Stanton Cemetery with Glenn Chapman, Zachary Blevins, Mike Reed, Gary Napier, Dwayne Hatton and Randall Young serving as active pallbearers. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Honorary pallbearers were Carol Jean and Dewey Hollon, George and Vickie Welicki, Vickie Reed, Karen and Tim Hatton, Kevin and Debbie Phelps, Gary Abner, Michelle Young, Josh and Heather Abney, Samantha and Jace Miller, Ruby Napie
2 CONC r, James Ed Dennis, and Monica and Jimmy Miller. 
2 CONT
2 CONT The family requests in lieu of flowers, donations can be made to Tunnel to Towers Foundation, 2361 Hylan Boulevard, Staten Island, NY 10306.
