1 NOTE {geni:about_me} T/Sgt Walter P. Back attended high school for 4 years and was a crane-man. He volunteered for the Air Corps of the Army of the United States at Patterson Field, Fairfield, Ohio on 27 April 1942.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was the engineer and top turret gunner on B-17 "Lady Marylin" on a mission to bomb the U-boat pens in Wilhelmshaven, Germany.
2 CONT
2 CONT The airplane collided in mid-air with B-17 #42-3533. All crew members of both planes, twenty men in total, were killed.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was awarded the Purple Heart and Air Medal, posthumously.
2 CONT
