2 NOTE what neat photos....I don't remember Uncle Clyde much as I was 3 years old when he was killed, but I will never
3 CONT forget his funeral.  The church was packed and my Mom was up front and they did not want the kids up front but
3 CONT I was such a "momma's kid" that I cried and cried to get to her and only settled down when they let me stand on
3 CONT the pew seat so I could see the back of her head.  My Mom spoke so lovingly of all the sweetest things that Uncle
3 CONT Clyde did for her and she was devastated at his death.  I do remember Aunt Marie and what a sweet and stylish
3 CONT person she was and of course we called our cousins triplets because she dressed you all alike at times and it was
3 CONT so neat.  It is good to hear of your family and if you have never contacted my oldest brother Jim Calloway, he
3 CONT had wonderful things to say about his Uncle Clyde and Aunt Marie.  His email is
3 CONT <jccdanddvdtech@aol.com>
3 CONT thanks for inviting me to join in.  I live in Bradenton, Florida and am divorced after 34 years and no
3 CONT children.  Am still working parttime, trying to save money for a cabin in Alabama where my folks
3 CONT left each child 40 acres....and I sort of want to go back to my roots at least part time.
3 CONT take care and keep in touch.
3 CONT ella may "ellie" calloway harrison, youngest daughter of Gussie Kinder Calloway.
