1 NAME Caroline C. /Cooper/
2 GIVN Caroline C.
2 SURN Cooper
2 _MARNM Wills
1 SEX F
1 BIRT
2 DATE 12 OCT 1921
1 DEAT
2 DATE 31 OCT 2010
1 OCCU
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/134292980/caroline_c-wills
2 CONT
2 CONT She was one of seven children of the late Col. Avery John and Ona Caroline 'Carey' (Gibson) Cooper. She was born while her father was stationed at Ft. Leavenworth.
2 CONT
2 CONT After a childhood at several Army Posts, she graduated from Western High School in Washington, D.C. She lived most of her adult life in the Washington area, including forty years in McLean, VA.
2 CONT
2 CONT She was the third generation of women in her direct family line who were alumnae of Vassar. After graduating from Vassar College in 1943 with a major in mathematics, she worked for IBM in Washington, D.C.
2 CONT
2 CONT She and her husband had retired to Melbourne, Brevard County, FL.
2 CONT
2 CONT Survivors at the time of her death include her husband of 48 years, R.W. Wills, daughter Carey (Wills) Dixon and husband USCG Lt. Commander Richard H. Dixon, her grandson, Robert Wills Dixon and granddaughter, Abigail Caroline Dix
2 CONC on presently residing in Covington, La., one brother, Col. Richmond J. Cooper and wife Janet (Felton) Cooper of Alexandria, one sister in law, Virginia "Jenny" Cooper of Arlington, six nephews and one niece.
