1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Lt. General Kenneth Banks Cooper'''
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/31862059/kenneth_banks-cooper
2 CONT
2 CONT Kenneth Banks Cooper, business executive, former army officer, retired military officer. Decorated Legion of Merit (2), Distinguished Service Medal (2), D.D.S.M. Member Society Military Engrs, Army Navy Country Club.
2 CONT
2 CONT ''Background''
2 CONT
2 CONT Cooper, Kenneth Banks was born on November 12, 1923 in Fort Leavenworth, Kansas, United States. Son of Avery John and Ona Carey (Gibson) Cooper.
2 CONT
2 CONT ''Education''
2 CONT
2 CONT Bachelor of Science, United States Military Academy, 1944; Master of Science, Massachusetts Institute of Technology, 1951.
2 CONT
2 CONT ''Career''
2 CONT
2 CONT Commissioned 2nd Lieutenant, United States Army, 1944; advanced through grades to Lieutenant general, 1975; World World War II service in S. Pacific, Philippines, Japan, 1944-1946; assigned to, Manhattan Project-Armed Forces Speci
2 CONC al Weapon Project, New Mexico, Eniwetok, and Washington, 1946-1948; member nuclear weapons staff, Atomic Energy Commission, Washington, 1951-1955; nuclear weapons planning officer, Supreme Headquarters Allied Powers in Europe, Par
2 CONC is, 1955-1958; project manager, ballistic missile defense research, Advanced Research Projects Agency, Washington, 1959-1963; battalion commander, Korea, 1963-1964; director, Army Nuclear Power Program, 1965-1966; with, Defense Co
2 CONC mmittee Planning Group, 1966-1968; executive to Secretary of Army, 1968-1970; brigade commander, Vietnam, 1970-1971; deputy director civil works, Office Chief of Engineers, Washington, 1971-1972; assistant chief engineers, Office 
2 CONC Chief of Engineers, Washington, 1972-1975; deputy commander-in-chief, United States Army, Europe, Heidelberg, Germany, 1975-1977; deputy adviser to Secretary of Defense, 1977-1978; retired, 1978; general manager Svc. and Construct
2 CONC ion Group, ITT, Nutley, New Jersey, 1978-1979; deputy assistant secretary defense for plans and resources, Office Assistant Secretary Defense Command, Control, Communications & Intelligence, Washington, 1980-1981; president, SPC I
2 CONC nternational, Arlington, Virginia, 1981-1984; consultant, BMD (Ballistic Missile Defense, formerly SDI), Alexandria, Virginia, 1985-1988; consultant, Institute Defense Analysis, since 1988.
2 CONT
2 CONT ''Achievements''
2 CONT
2 CONT Kenneth Banks Cooper has been listed as a noteworthy Business executive, army officer by Marquis Who's Who.
2 CONT
2 CONT ''Membership''
2 CONT
2 CONT Member Society Military Engrs, Army Navy Country Club.
2 CONT
2 CONT ''Connections''
2 CONT
2 CONT Married Virginia Leah Adkins, December 29, 1979. Children by previous marriage to Barbara Agnes Nesbit: Kenneth, Robert.
2 CONT
2 CONT Father:
2 CONT
2 CONT Avery John Cooper
2 CONT
2 CONT Mother:
2 CONT
2 CONT Ona Carey (Gibson) Cooper
