1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Valdosta Daily Times
2 CONT Obituaries for Sunday, June 10, 2007
2 CONT
2 CONT Eunice Wade Williams
2 CONT
2 CONT Eunice Wade Williams, 86, of Valdosta, died Friday, June 8, 2007 at Fellowship Home. She was born on Feb. 9, 1921, in Lake Park to the late William Hannibal and Estelle Carter Wade and was a lifelong resident of Lowndes County. Mr
2 CONC s. Williams was a member of the First Christian Church and retired from sales at Sears.
2 CONT
2 CONT Survivors include her son and daughter-in-law, J. Kenneth and Becky Flythe of Valdosta; stepson and stepdaughter-in-law, Clark B., Jr. and Celia Williams of Lizella; stepdaughters and stepsons in law, Doris and Alfred Scott of Peo
2 CONC ria, Ariz., and Jane and C. W. Kirby of Merrimack, N.H.; three grandchildren, Dale Keith and Teresa Flythe, Mark Allen and Penny Flythe and Deidra Flythe DiPietro; five great grandchildren; eight stepgrandchildren; one brother, Ar
2 CONC thur Wade of West Palm Beach, Fla. She was preceded in death by her husband, Clark B. Williams Sr.; a son, John Wade Flythe; her former husband, James Edward Flythe; two brothers, Carter Wade and Pierce Wade; and a half-sister, In
2 CONC a Golden.
2 CONT
2 CONT Funeral services will be held at 11 a.m. Monday, June 11, 2007, in the chapel of Carson McLane Funeral Home with the Rev. Charlie Scarborough officiating. Burial will follow in Riverview Memorial Gardens. The family will receive f
2 CONC riends on Sunday from 6-8 p.m.. at the funeral home. Condolences to the family may be conveyed online at www.mclanefuneralservivces.com. -Carson McLane Funeral Home.
2 CONT * Reference: [https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/96683008/eunice-williams Find A Grave Memorial] - [https://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Jan 15 2023, 16:38:10 UTC''
