1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Columbus Republic 17 May 2002
2 CONT Clarice E. George
2 CONT Road 550S
2 CONT
2 CONT Clarice E. George, 81, of Road 550S died at 4:15 a.m. Thursday, May 16, 2002, at Major Hospital in Shelbyville.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mrs. George was an avid flower gardener and walker.
2 CONT
2 CONT The funeral will be at 1:30 p.m. Monday at Barkes, Inlow & Weaver Funeral Home on Washington Street, with the Rev. Hugh Severance officiating. Calling will be from 2 to 5 p.m. Sunday and from 12:30 p.m. until service time Monday. 
2 CONC Burial will be at Bethel Baptist Cemetery.
2 CONT
2 CONT Memorials may be made to the Alzheimer's Association.
2 CONT
2 CONT Born in Russell Springs, Ky., Jan. 1, 1921, Mrs. George was the daughter of Grover C. and Ella Flanigan Brown. She married Tobias I. George in 1941. He died May 4, 1998.
2 CONT
2 CONT Survivors include a son, Gary George of Greenfield; a daughter, Pandora Eads of Kansas City, Mo.; a brother, Arnese Brown of Russell Springs; sisters, Loa Blankenship and Janet Foley, both of Russell Springs; grandchildren, Mike, 
2 CONC Steve, John and Madelynn George, Brian Brown, Amy Bird, David Eads, Barri Grieger and Angie Trice; and nine great-grandchildren.
2 CONT
2 CONT She was preceded in death by a brother, Olive Brown, and sisters, Gladys Brown, Cora Bennett, Margie Blankenship and Nelia Wilson.* Reference: [https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/65064468/clarice-e-george Find A Grave Memorial] -
