1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Paul West, age 85 years, of the Thompson-Hood Veterans Center in Wilmore, Kentucky, formerly of Columbia, Kentucky, passed away Monday, February 12, 2007 at 6:07 a.m. at the Veterans Hospital in Lexington, Kentucky
2 CONC  after an illness. He was the son of the late Oscar and Armilda Rich West of Adair County, Kentucky. Besides his parents, he was also preceded in death by five brothers: Raymond, Joe, Hershel, Floyd, and Lonzie West and by four si
2 CONC sters: Eva Bernard, Letha Dickerson, Lola Bell West, and Stella Wingler. Mr. West was married to Lucille Ellis West for 25 years. He is survived by two sons, Freeman West and his wife, Joyce, of Columbia, Kentucky and Richard West
2 CONC  of Lexington, Kentucky, and two daughters, Phyllis Gooden of Columbia, Kentucky and Nancy Ellis and her husband, Kelly, of Columbia, Kentucky; one brother, Robert Scott West of Cincinnati, OH; one sister, Ruby Brown of Cincinnati
2 CONC , OH. Fourteen grandchildren and 12 great-grandchildren also survive. Mr. West was a U.S. Army Veteran of World War II and was a retired foundry worker from the Willard Bronze Company in Ohio. Funeral service was held on Wednesday
2 CONC , February 14, 2007 at 11:00 a.m. at Stotts-Phelps-McQueary Funeral Home with Rev. Travis Adams officiating. Interment in the Haven Hill Cemetery with military honors presented by Columbia VFW Post 6097. Pallbearers were: Daniel E
2 CONC llis, Eric Ellis, Shaun Gooden, Adam West, Gary West, Jason West, Jeremy West, and Ricky West. Expressions of sympathy may take the form of a donation to the Thompson-Hood Veterans Center, 100 Veterans Drive, Wilmore, KY 40390. Th
2 CONC is obituary may be viewed on and a guest book signed online at stottsphelpsmcquearyfh.com. Stotts-Phelps-McQueary Funeral Home was in charge of funeral arrangements. 
