0 @N6000000001574502175@ NOTE Susan Boydston (susanb@cysource.com) records William as the III, but his grandfather is Nathaniel. It may be that the father was named the II after his great-grandfather, as Susan suggests, or to distinguish him from another Willi
1 CONC am, but for simplicity's sake, I retain Sr. and Jr. for this father and son.
1 CONT
1 CONT It is Susan Boydston who provides the additional children of the couple and also more complete information on the two I had entered before -- Willie and John Lee.
1 CONT
1 CONT Sharon McAllister (Lutherok@cs.com) wrote in May 2001 that she had located William (and provides a middle initial "R") in Dewey Township, just south of Luther, Oklahoma. This was a census record, apparently the 1900 US Census, alt
1 CONC hough she merely says that the census showed the couple had been married 2 years, and had one child, still living.
0 @N6000000001574603936@ NOTE Cemetery Records of Platte County, Missouri, Vol. 2 p. 11 lists a Willie Boydston b. 7 Apr 1855 and died 19 May 1925.
1 CONT
1 CONT Information on the Lee/Willie Boydston listed with this family comes through Ruth Walton from Dorothy Naylor and indicates that Willie died 27 Oct 1972. The information continues "Willie Boydston, son of Will Boydston, was a cousi
1 CONC n to Wesley Boydston.  Will Boydston Sr. and Nathaniel Boydston were brothers."  She adds that Willie's wife was named Wilda, and their children included Claude Boydston who married Marie Smith.
1 CONT
1 CONT Of the numerous Nathaniel and William Boydstons, this is the only combination that fits the circumstance described above.
1 CONT
1 CONT Susan Boydston (susanb@cysource.com) sends in March 2000 information that this child is named William "Willy" IV (see notes on the father) and was born 30 oct 1879 and died 26 Oct 1972. She further gives information on Lee born 7 
1 CONC Apr 1877 died 18 May 1925, buried in Missouri. She states that "Willy" married Wilda Montgomery.
1 CONT
1 CONT This should lay to rest the confusion encountered early along.
1 CONT
1 CONT Susan lists "Willy" as William IV, but once again, since a generation is skipped, I have made the decision for now to list as III, indicating consecutive generations, to avoid confusion.
1 CONT
1 CONT Sharon McAllister (Lutherok@cs.com) adds the middle initial "R." in her correspondence of May 2001.
0 @N6000000001574945659@ NOTE John Lee Boydstun took his own life in his farm house in Rushville, Missouri. He was suffering from fluid on his lungs.
